(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const q=(prompt,answer,d1,d2,explain,sense=1,type='meaning')=>({prompt,answer,d1,d2,explain,sense,type});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:'Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/'+w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')});
const P=(w,origin,c,m,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(c)?c:[c],mistakes:[m],quiz:qs.map((x,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+x.sense,type:'辨义与用法',prompt:x.prompt,options:[x.answer,x.d1,x.d2],answer:x.answer,explain:x.explain,errorType:x.type}))});
P('self-serving','Self-serving combines self and serving; the adjective describes conduct or statements aimed at one’s own advantage, often at others’ expense.',C('self-serving.s1','动机与行为','The director’s self-serving report praised his own decisions but omitted the safety failures that harmed workers.','主管那份只图己利的报告夸赞自己的决定，却略去了伤害工人的安全事故。','The director’s self-serving report / praised his decisions / but omitted the failures.','self-serving.s1 描述主要为了个人利益而做的事或说的话。','报告只挑有利于主管的内容。'),M('The director’s self-serving report put workers’ needs first and disclosed facts that damaged his own reputation.','The director’s self-serving report protected his own interests by omitting harmful facts.','主动揭露损害自身的事实、优先照顾工人，不符合只图己利。','meaning'),[q('What did the director’s report leave out?','the safety failures that harmed workers','his own praise and favorable decisions','the meeting date','报告略去了伤害工人的安全事故。',1,'context'),q('Whose decisions did the report praise?','the director’s own decisions','the workers’ suggestions','the inspector’s findings','报告夸赞的是主管自己的决定。',1,'context'),q('What does self-serving suggest about the report?','it was designed to benefit its author','it was written to protect every worker','it was an impartial safety manual','self-serving 表示主要为了作者自身利益。',1,'meaning'),q('Which action is self-serving?','hiding failures to preserve one’s own position','revealing a mistake that could harm one’s career','sharing credit fairly with the whole team','为保住自己的职位而隐瞒失败属于 self-serving。',1,'context')]);
P('self-sufficiency','Self-sufficiency is formed from self and sufficiency; it means the condition of needing no outside supply, money, or support.',C('self-sufficiency.s1','自足','The island’s plan for self-sufficiency included growing staple crops and storing rainwater through the dry season.','这座岛的自给计划包括种植主粮，并储存雨季雨水以度过旱季。','The plan for self-sufficiency included growing crops / and storing water / through the dry season.','self-sufficiency.s1 指不依赖外部物资、资金或援助的状态。','岛上计划依靠本地生产和储水。'),M('The island achieved self-sufficiency by importing every meal and relying on outside aid for all water.','The island pursued self-sufficiency by growing food and storing its own water.','完全依赖进口和外援不符合自足。','meaning'),[q('What did the island plan to grow?','staple crops','tea for export only','flowers for a festival','岛上计划种植主粮。',1,'context'),q('How would it prepare for the dry season?','by storing rainwater','by importing all its water','by closing the wells','储存雨水能帮助岛上度过旱季。',1,'context'),q('What is self-sufficiency?','a state of needing no outside supply or support','a rule requiring all goods to be imported','a temporary shortage of food','self-sufficiency 指不依赖外部供应或援助的状态。',1,'meaning'),q('Which community shows self-sufficiency?','one that produces its food and manages its own water','one that depends on another region for every meal','one that has no plan for essential supplies','能生产食物并管理水源的社区体现 self-sufficiency。',1,'context')]);
P('self-sufficient','Self-sufficient combines self and sufficient; it describes a person, community, or country able to provide needed goods and resources without outside help.',C('self-sufficient.s1','自给自足的','The cooperative became self-sufficient after its members built a greenhouse and repaired the village well.','合作社成员建好温室并修复村井后，合作社实现了自给自足。','The cooperative became self-sufficient / after building a greenhouse / and repairing its well.','self-sufficient.s1 指能够自行生产或获得所需资源而不靠外援。','温室和井帮助合作社满足自身需要。'),M('The village was self-sufficient because it could not produce anything and depended on daily deliveries from elsewhere.','The village was self-sufficient because it produced food and maintained its own water supply.','每天依赖外地送货说明并非自给自足。','meaning'),[q('What helped the cooperative become self-sufficient?','a greenhouse and a repaired village well','a new road for daily imports','a contract to buy all food elsewhere','合作社建了温室并修好村井。',1,'context'),q('What could the cooperative provide more independently?','food and water','foreign currency only','a city bus service','温室和井让合作社更能自给食物与水。',1,'context'),q('What does self-sufficient describe?','able to provide needed resources without outside help','unable to meet any needs alone','willing to sell everything abroad','self-sufficient 指无需外援即可满足所需。',1,'meaning'),q('Which farm is self-sufficient?','one that grows its own food and supplies its own water','one that imports every crop and all drinking water','one that has no source of food','自行种植粮食并提供用水的农场是 self-sufficient。',1,'context')]);
P('self-sustaining','Self-sustaining combines self and sustaining; it describes a system that continues through its own resources.',C('self-sustaining.s1','自持的；自我维持的','The wetland became self-sustaining once native plants returned and the restored stream flowed year-round.','本地植物恢复生长、溪流全年不断后，这片湿地便能自我维持。','The wetland became self-sustaining / once native plants returned / and the stream flowed year-round.','self-sustaining.s1 指依靠自身资源持续存在或运行。','恢复的生态系统能维持自身。'),M('The wetland was self-sustaining only while workers supplied all its water and replanted every day.','The wetland was self-sustaining because its restored stream and native plants maintained the ecosystem.','必须每天靠人力补给才能继续，说明它尚不能自我维持。','meaning'),[q('What allowed the wetland to become self-sustaining?','native plants returned and the stream flowed year-round','workers supplied water every morning','all wildlife was removed','本地植物恢复、溪流全年不断，湿地得以自我维持。',1,'context'),q('How long did the restored stream flow?','year-round','only during one afternoon','only after workers poured water','溪流全年不断。',1,'context'),q('What does self-sustaining mean?','continuing through a system’s own resources','depending on constant outside supplies','stopping whenever outside help ends','self-sustaining 指依靠自身资源持续存在。',1,'meaning'),q('Which garden is self-sustaining?','one whose plants reseed and whose water cycle maintains the beds','one that survives only with daily outside deliveries','one that has been abandoned and is dying','能自行繁殖并靠自身水循环维持的花园是 self-sustaining。',1,'context')]);
P('selfish','Selfish is built from self and -ish; it means caring only about oneself or doing something mainly for personal advantage.',[C('selfish.s1','自私的；只顾自己','It was selfish of Omar to take the last seat while an injured passenger was still standing.','受伤乘客还站着，奥马尔却占了最后一个座位，这很自私。','It was selfish of Omar / to take the last seat / while an injured passenger stood.','selfish.s1 指只关心自己而不顾他人。','他只顾自己坐下，不理会受伤乘客。'),C('selfish.s2','利己的；为个人好处的','The donation looked generous, but the company made it for selfish reasons: the gift secured a profitable contract.','这笔捐赠看似慷慨，但公司的动机是利己的：捐赠换来了一份有利可图的合同。','The company donated for selfish reasons / because the gift secured / a profitable contract.','selfish.s2 也可形容主要为了自身好处而做的动机或行为。','捐赠是为了获得合同。')],M('Omar was selfish when he gave his seat to the injured passenger and waited for the next bus.','Omar was selfish when he took the last seat while the injured passenger remained standing.','让座照顾伤者并非只顾自己。','meaning'),[q('Why was Omar’s action selfish?','he took the last seat while an injured passenger stood','he offered the injured passenger his seat','he waited for the next bus','奥马尔占了最后一个座位，没顾及受伤乘客。',1,'context'),q('Why did the company make the donation?','to secure a profitable contract','to remain anonymous and gain nothing','because the contract had already been canceled','公司捐赠是为了获得有利可图的合同。',2,'context'),q('What does selfish mean in the seat example?','caring only about one’s own comfort','putting an injured person first','giving away one’s own seat','此处 selfish 指只顾自己的舒适。',1,'meaning'),q('What does selfish describe in “selfish reasons”?','motives aimed mainly at personal advantage','a decision made solely for public benefit','a gift with no possible return','selfish reasons 指主要出于个人好处的动机。',2,'meaning')]);
P('selfishness','Selfishness is formed from selfish and -ness; it means behavior that puts one’s own wishes first while ignoring other people.',C('selfishness.s1','利己；任性自私','The team’s selfishness showed when each player refused to pass the ball to a teammate in a better position.','每名队员都不肯把球传给位置更好的队友，球队的自私由此显现。','The team’s selfishness showed / when each player refused / to pass to a teammate.','selfishness.s1 指优先满足自己的愿望而忽视他人的行为。','队员只顾个人表现、不顾队友。'),M('The team’s selfishness was clear because every player shared the ball and put the group’s result first.','The team’s selfishness was clear because players refused to pass to better-positioned teammates.','无私分享并把团队放在首位，不是 selfishness。','meaning'),[q('How did the players show selfishness?','they refused to pass to teammates in better positions','they passed whenever a teammate was free','they left the ball with the referee','队员拒绝传球给位置更好的队友。',1,'context'),q('What did each player prioritize?','individual possession','the team’s shared result','the opponent’s comfort','每名队员优先考虑自己持球。',1,'context'),q('What is selfishness?','behavior that puts one’s own wishes first and ignores others','a habit of sharing resources fairly','a plan to help every teammate','selfishness 指只顾自己而忽视他人的行为。',1,'meaning'),q('Which decision shows selfishness?','keeping a needed tool while a coworker has none','sharing the only tool with the coworker','taking turns so both can finish','同事没有工具却把唯一工具留给自己，体现 selfishness。',1,'context')]);
P('selfless','Selfless is formed from self and -less; it means thinking of others first or willingly giving up one’s own comfort or safety for them.',[C('selfless.s1','无私的','The selfless nurse stayed late to comfort frightened patients after her shift had officially ended.','这名无私的护士在下班后留下来安慰受惊的病人。','The selfless nurse stayed late / to comfort frightened patients / after her shift.','selfless.s1 指把他人放在自己之前。','护士优先照顾病人。'),C('selfless.s2','不顾自己的；舍己的','In a selfless rescue, the firefighter entered the smoke-filled room to carry an unconscious child outside.','在一次舍己救援中，消防员进入浓烟弥漫的房间，把昏迷的孩子抱了出来。','In a selfless rescue, the firefighter entered the smoke-filled room / to carry a child outside.','selfless.s2 强调愿意为他人放弃自己的舒适或安全。','消防员冒险救出孩子。')],M('The nurse acted selflessly by refusing to help any patient and leaving early for her own convenience.','The nurse acted selflessly by staying late to comfort the patients.','拒绝帮助他人、只顾自己不属于无私。','meaning'),[q('What did the nurse do after her shift?','stayed late to comfort frightened patients','left early without speaking to anyone','asked patients to comfort her','护士下班后留下安慰病人。',1,'context'),q('What risk did the firefighter take?','entering a smoke-filled room to rescue a child','avoiding the building and leaving the child inside','waiting for the child to carry the firefighter','消防员冒险进入浓烟房间救孩子。',2,'context'),q('What does selfless mean in the nursing example?','putting other people’s needs before one’s own','seeking praise for refusing to help','protecting only one’s own convenience','此处 selfless 指优先考虑他人。',1,'meaning'),q('What does selfless emphasize in the rescue?','willingness to risk personal safety for another person','a refusal to enter any dangerous place','a plan to receive a reward','救援句中的 selfless 强调为他人舍弃自身安全。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sell','Sell comes from Old English sellan (“give, furnish”); it can mean exchange goods for money, be bought in stated numbers, or persuade people to accept an idea.',[C('sell.s1','卖；出售','The farm sells fresh eggs at the Saturday market in exchange for cash or card payment.','农场在周六集市出售新鲜鸡蛋，接受现金或刷卡付款。','The farm sells fresh eggs / at the Saturday market / for payment.','sell.s1 指把商品交给买方以换取金钱。','鸡蛋以付款为条件出售。'),C('sell.s2','有销路；售出','The first edition sold 40,000 copies during its opening month, so the publisher ordered a reprint.','首版在上市首月售出四万册，因此出版社下令重印。','The first edition sold 40,000 copies / during its opening month / prompting a reprint.','sell.s2 指商品被买走并达到某个销量。','书作为商品售出了四万册。'),C('sell.s3','推销；使接受','The presenter used clear cost figures to sell the proposal to a skeptical city council.','陈述者用清晰的成本数据说服持怀疑态度的市议会接受提案。','The presenter used cost figures / to sell the proposal / to the council.','sell.s3 指说服别人相信某个主意或接受某项计划。','数据帮助陈述者说服议会。')],M('The farm sells eggs by giving them away for free and receiving no payment from anyone.','The farm sells eggs in exchange for money.','免费赠送而不收款不是 sell 的“出售”义。','meaning'),[q('Where does the farm sell its eggs?','at the Saturday market','at the city council meeting','inside the publisher’s office','农场在周六集市出售鸡蛋。',1,'context'),q('How many copies sold in the opening month?','40,000','4,000','400,000','首版上市首月售出四万册。',2,'context'),q('What does sell mean when the presenter sells a proposal?','persuade people to accept an idea','exchange a physical item for cash only','record how many books were bought','此处 sell 指说服他人接受提案。',3,'meaning'),q('What does “the book sold well” mean?','many copies were bought by readers','the author persuaded a council to vote','the publisher gave every copy away','the book sold well 表示读者买了很多册。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sell abroad','Sell abroad is the verb sell plus the adverb abroad; it means offer and sell goods or services in countries other than one’s own.',C('sell abroad.s1','在国外销售；出口','The small dairy began to sell abroad after meeting the labeling and food-safety rules of neighboring countries.','这家小型乳品厂满足邻国的标签和食品安全规定后，开始向国外销售产品。','The dairy began to sell abroad / after meeting neighboring countries’ / labeling and safety rules.','sell abroad.s1 指向本国以外的国家销售商品或服务。','乳品厂遵守邻国规定后向国外销售。'),M('The dairy began to sell abroad by delivering its products only to customers inside its home country.','The dairy began to sell abroad by exporting its products to neighboring countries.','只在本国境内销售不属于 sell abroad。','meaning'),[q('What did the dairy need to meet before selling abroad?','neighboring countries’ labeling and food-safety rules','the city council’s election schedule','a rule banning exports','乳品厂先满足邻国的标签与食品安全规定。',1,'context'),q('Where did the dairy begin to sell its products?','in countries beyond its own','only in its home village','only at one local farm','这家乳品厂开始向本国以外的国家销售产品。',1,'context'),q('What does sell abroad mean?','to offer goods or services for sale in other countries','to sell goods only to local customers','to buy foreign goods for personal use','sell abroad 指在其他国家销售商品或服务。',1,'meaning'),q('Which company sells abroad?','a local maker exporting its cheese to three neighboring countries','a shop serving customers only in its own town','a buyer ordering imports for its own use','把奶酪出口到邻国的本地厂商是在 sell abroad。',1,'context')]);
P('sell for','Sell for combines sell with for; it means to be sold at a particular price.',C('sell for.s1','卖得；售价为','The signed first-edition novel sold for $2,400 at the charity auction.','这本签名初版小说在慈善拍卖会上卖了2400美元。','The signed novel sold for $2,400 / at the auction / for charity.','sell for.s1 表示商品以某个金额售出。','句中 for 后接实际成交价。'),M('The signed novel sold for $2,400, but the auction record says the buyer paid nothing.','The signed novel sold for $2,400 at the auction.','成交价与实际付款金额必须一致。','meaning'),[q('How much did the signed novel sell for?','$2,400','$240','$24,000','签名初版小说卖了2400美元。',1,'context'),q('Where was the book sold?','at a charity auction','at a neighborhood dairy','in a foreign school semester','这本书在慈善拍卖会上售出。',1,'context'),q('What does sell for introduce?','the amount a thing is sold at','the country where a seller lives','the reason a buyer reads a book','sell for 后面说明商品的售价。',1,'meaning'),q('Which sentence correctly uses sell for?','The painting sold for $800.','The painting sold for across the room.','The painting sold for very slowly.','“The painting sold for $800”中的 for 后接售价，搭配正确。',1,'grammar')]);
P('seller','Seller is formed from sell and the agent suffix -er; it means a person or business offering goods for sale, or a product sold in large numbers.',[C('seller.s1','卖方；销售者','The seller disclosed the repaired roof and gave the buyer copies of the inspection reports.','卖方说明屋顶修缮情况，并把检查报告副本交给买方。','The seller disclosed the repair / and gave the buyer / inspection reports.','seller.s1 指提供商品或房屋出售的人、公司或商店。','卖方把房屋情况告知买方。'),C('seller.s2','畅销品','The publisher called the cookbook a bestseller after it remained among the top-selling titles for six months.','这本食谱连续六个月位居畅销书榜前列，出版社因此称它为畅销品。','The cookbook became a bestseller / after staying among / top-selling titles for six months.','seller.s2 可指销量很大的书或产品。','cookbook 是销量很大的商品。')],M('The seller hid the roof repairs from the buyer and refused to provide the inspection report.','The seller disclosed the roof repairs and provided the inspection report.','卖方隐瞒维修情况与源例中的诚实披露相反。','meaning'),[q('What did the seller give the buyer?','copies of the inspection reports','a recipe book ranking','a semicolon guide','卖方把检查报告副本交给买方。',1,'context'),q('Why did the publisher call the cookbook a bestseller?','it stayed among top-selling titles for six months','it was never bought by readers','it was sold abroad once','这本食谱连续六个月位列畅销书。',2,'context'),q('What is a seller in the house example?','a person offering a property for sale','a buyer who pays for a house','a book with high sales','第一句 seller 指出售房屋的一方。',1,'meaning'),q('What does seller mean in “a bestseller”?','a product or book sold in large numbers','a person who checks property repairs','a store that refuses to sell books','bestseller 中的 seller 指销量很大的商品。',2,'meaning')]);
P('selling','Selling is the -ing form of sell and a noun for the activity or business of offering goods or services for money.',C('selling.s1','销售；出售活动','Selling handmade lamps online became Mei’s full-time business after demand grew beyond the weekend market.','需求超过周末集市后，梅在网上销售手工灯具成了全职生意。','Selling handmade lamps online / became Mei’s full-time business / as demand grew.','selling.s1 指为换取金钱而提供商品或服务的活动或业务。','在线销售灯具成为她的生意。'),M('Selling handmade lamps means giving every lamp away and never offering one to a customer for payment.','Selling handmade lamps means offering them to customers in exchange for money.','不给顾客出售商品不属于 selling。','meaning'),[q('What did Mei sell online?','handmade lamps','signed novels','dairy products','梅在网上销售手工灯具。',1,'context'),q('What caused the online business to become full-time?','demand grew beyond the weekend market','the lamps stopped attracting buyers','the business ended after one day','需求超过周末集市后，梅把网上销售变成全职生意。',1,'context'),q('What does selling mean here?','the business activity of offering goods for payment','the act of buying goods for personal use','a method for measuring a semester','selling 指以收款为目的提供商品的业务活动。',1,'meaning'),q('Which activity is selling?','offering handmade lamps to customers for money','giving lamps away without offering them for purchase','repairing the roof of a house one owns','把手工灯具提供给顾客购买属于 selling。',1,'context')]);
P('semantic','Semantic comes from Greek sēmantikos (“significant”), from sēmainein (“to signify”); it concerns meaning rather than sound or grammar, or the study of meaning.',[C('semantic.s1','语义的','Changing “not” to “now” creates a semantic difference because the two words express different meanings.','把“not”改成“now”会造成语义差异，因为两个词表达的意思不同。','Changing “not” to “now” creates a semantic difference / because the words / mean different things.','semantic.s1 指与词语含义有关，而非声音或语法形式。','改词后含义改变。'),C('semantic.s2','语义学的','Her semantic research examines how context changes the meaning listeners assign to an ambiguous phrase.','她的语义学研究考察语境如何改变听者赋予一个歧义短语的含义。','Her semantic research examines / how context changes meaning / in an ambiguous phrase.','semantic.s2 指属于语言意义研究的语义学领域。','研究关注语境与含义。')],M('Replacing “not” with “now” makes no semantic difference because both words have exactly the same meaning.','Replacing “not” with “now” changes the semantic meaning of the sentence.','not 与 now 含义不同，替换会改变语义。','meaning'),[q('Why does replacing “not” with “now” change the sentence?','the words express different meanings','their sounds and meanings are identical','the sentence becomes a question','两个词含义不同，所以替换会造成语义差异。',1,'context'),q('What does the researcher examine?','how context affects the meaning of an ambiguous phrase','how to repair a greenhouse','how sellers set auction prices','研究考察语境如何影响歧义短语的含义。',2,'context'),q('What does semantic mean in “semantic difference”?','related to meaning in language','related only to pronunciation','related to punctuation marks','semantic difference 指语义差异。',1,'meaning'),q('What does semantic mean in “semantic research”?','belonging to the study of meaning','belonging to the study of plant growth','belonging to the study of selling goods','semantic research 指语义学研究。',2,'meaning')]);
P('semantically','Semantically is formed from semantic and -ally; it means in terms of meaning in language.',C('semantically.s1','在意义上','The two instructions are semantically similar, although one is phrased as a command and the other as a polite request.','这两条指令在意义上相近，尽管一条写成命令，另一条写成礼貌请求。','The instructions are semantically similar / although their phrasing / differs in politeness.','semantically.s1 指从语言意义的角度或层面来看。','措辞语气不同，但表达的意思接近。'),M('The instructions are semantically identical because they use the same font, even though one says “open” and the other says “close.”','The instructions are not semantically identical because “open” and “close” have opposite meanings.','字体相同不决定语义；open 与 close 含义相反。','meaning'),[q('In what way are the instructions similar?','in their meaning','in their font size','in their punctuation only','两条指令在表达的意义上相近。',1,'context'),q('How does their phrasing differ?','one is a command and one is a polite request','one is in English and one is in silence','one is a price and one is a location','一条是命令，另一条是礼貌请求。',1,'context'),q('What does semantically mean?','in terms of meaning in language','in terms of spelling length','in terms of a seller’s income','semantically 指从语言意义层面来看。',1,'meaning'),q('Which pair is semantically similar?','“Please sit down” and “Have a seat”','“open the door” and “close the door”','“three dollars” and “three miles”','“Please sit down”和“Have a seat”表达的意思相近。',1,'context')]);
P('semantics','Semantics is from Greek sēmantikos (“significant”) and names the branch of linguistics concerned with meaning, as distinct from syntax.',C('semantics.s1','语义；语义学','The class compared semantics with syntax by asking what each sentence means and how its words are arranged.','课堂通过讨论每个句子的含义及词语排列方式，比较了语义学与句法学。','The class compared semantics with syntax / by asking what sentences mean / and how words are arranged.','semantics.s1 指研究语言意义的语言学分支，也指与句法相对的意义层面。','课程把句意与词序作为两类研究对象。'),M('Semantics studies only the order of words and ignores what sentences mean.','Semantics studies meaning, while syntax concerns how words are arranged.','只研究词序而不研究意义描述的是句法，不是语义学。','meaning'),[q('What did the class ask about sentences?','what each sentence means','how much each book sells for','whether the room is semicircular','课堂讨论每个句子的含义。',1,'context'),q('What did they compare with semantics?','syntax','self-sufficiency','the seller’s price','他们将 semantics 与 syntax 作比较。',1,'context'),q('What is semantics?','the branch of linguistics that studies meaning','the branch that studies only word order','a mark that separates clauses','semantics 指研究语言意义的分支。',1,'meaning'),q('Which question belongs most directly to semantics?','What does this sentence mean?','Which word comes second in the sentence?','How many letters are in the sentence?','“这个句子是什么意思？”直接询问语义。',1,'context')]);
P('semblance','Semblance comes from Old French semblance, from sembler (“seem, appear”); it means an outward appearance, especially one unlike the reality.',C('semblance.s1','外表；貌似','After the storm, the volunteers restored a semblance of order by clearing the road and marking safe routes.','暴风雨过后，志愿者清理道路并标出安全路线，使现场恢复了些许秩序的样子。','The volunteers restored a semblance of order / by clearing the road / and marking routes.','semblance.s1 指事物外在呈现的样子，尤其暗示真实情况可能不同。','他们恢复了表面上的秩序。'),M('The volunteers restored a semblance of order by leaving every road blocked and every warning sign missing.','The volunteers restored a semblance of order by clearing roads and marking safe routes.','道路仍堵塞、警示全无，无法呈现秩序的样子。','meaning'),[q('What did the volunteers clear?','the road','the town’s semester schedule','the auction room','志愿者清理了道路。',1,'context'),q('What did they mark after the storm?','safe routes','the storm’s sale prices','a semicircle on the road','他们标出安全路线。',1,'context'),q('What does semblance mean?','an outward appearance or show','a reliable measurement of rainfall','a complete account of every fact','semblance 指外表或表面呈现出的样子。',1,'meaning'),q('Why can “a semblance of order” imply the situation is not fully orderly?','semblance can mean only an appearance, not necessarily the full reality','semblance always means perfect order','the phrase refers to a school term','semblance 可指表面样子，未必代表真实情况完全如此。',1,'meaning')]);
P('semester','Semester comes from Latin semestris (“six-monthly”), from sex (“six”) and mensis (“month”); it is half of an academic year.',C('semester.s1','学期','The registrar moved the chemistry course to the spring semester so students could finish its laboratory sequence.','教务员把化学课调到春季学期，以便学生完成实验课程安排。','The registrar moved the course / to the spring semester / for the laboratory sequence.','semester.s1 指学校或大学学年的一半。','课程被安排到春季学期。'),M('The registrar called a single afternoon lecture a full semester of study.','The registrar placed the course in the spring semester, one half of the academic year.','一堂下午课不能等同于一个完整学期。','meaning'),[q('Which course was moved?','chemistry','semantics','a self-sufficiency seminar','教务员调整的是化学课。',1,'context'),q('To which semester was it moved?','the spring semester','the winter solstice','the final week only','课程被调到春季学期。',1,'context'),q('What is a semester?','half of a school or college year','a single lecture lasting one hour','a six-day school week','semester 指学校学年的一半。',1,'meaning'),q('How many semesters usually divide an academic year?','two','fourteen','one hundred','一个学年通常分为两个 semester。',1,'meaning')]);
P('semiarid','Semiarid combines semi- (“partly”) and arid (“dry”); it describes a dry climate or region that still supports some grass or scrub.',C('semiarid.s1','半干旱的','The semiarid plateau receives little rain, but seasonal grasses still provide grazing after spring showers.','这片半干旱高原雨水稀少，但春季阵雨后仍会长出可供放牧的季节性草地。','The semiarid plateau receives little rain / but seasonal grasses grow / after spring showers.','semiarid.s1 描述干旱但仍能生长少量草或灌木的气候与地区。','少雨地区仍有季节性草地。'),M('The semiarid plateau receives heavy rain every day and is covered by dense tropical forest.','The semiarid plateau is dry but supports some seasonal grass.','每日暴雨与茂密热带雨林不符合半干旱气候。','meaning'),[q('How much rain does the plateau receive?','little rain','heavy rain every day','no rain under any condition','高原雨水稀少。',1,'context'),q('What grows after spring showers?','seasonal grasses','dense tropical forest','saltwater coral','春雨后会长出季节性草地。',1,'context'),q('What does semiarid describe?','dry regions that still support some vegetation','places that receive constant heavy rain','land where nothing can ever grow','semiarid 指干燥但仍有少量植被生长的地区。',1,'meaning'),q('Which landscape is semiarid?','a dry plain with scattered grass after seasonal rain','a rainforest with daily downpours','a lifeless area where no plant can grow','季节性降雨后有零星草地的干旱平原属于半干旱地区。',1,'context')]);
P('semicircular','Semicircular combines semi- (“half”) and circular; it describes a half-circle shape or an arrangement following that curve.',C('semicircular.s1','半圆的','The audience sat in a semicircular row around the small platform so every person could see the speaker.','观众围着小讲台排成半圆形，使每个人都能看到演讲者。','The audience sat in a semicircular row / around the platform / so everyone could see.','semicircular.s1 指呈半圆形或沿半圆曲线排列。','座位沿半圆弧排列。'),M('The audience formed a semicircular row by standing in four straight lines that made a rectangle.','The audience sat in a curved half-circle around the platform.','矩形的四条直线不是半圆弧形。','meaning'),[q('How were the seats arranged?','in a curved row around the platform','in four lines forming a rectangle','in a complete circle around the street','观众围绕讲台排成弧形。',1,'context'),q('Why was the row semicircular?','it followed a half-circle curve','it formed a square','it had no curved section','座位排列沿着半圆曲线。',1,'context'),q('What does semicircular mean?','shaped like half of a circle','shaped like a full square','having no curve at all','semicircular 指半圆形的。',1,'meaning'),q('Which arrangement is semicircular?','chairs following a half-circle arc','chairs forming a complete rectangle','chairs scattered without a curve','沿半圆弧排列的椅子是 semicircular。',1,'context')]);
P('semicolon','Semicolon combines semi- (“partly”) and colon, ultimately from Greek kōlon (“clause”); it is the punctuation mark ;, stronger than a comma but weaker than a full stop.',C('semicolon.s1','分号（；）','The editor joined the closely related clauses with a semicolon; the second clause could still stand as a sentence.','编辑用分号连接关系密切的分句；第二个分句仍可独立成句。','The editor joined related clauses with a semicolon / and the second clause / could stand alone.','semicolon.s1 是分隔力度强于逗号、弱于句号的标点符号。','分号连接相关且可独立的分句。'),M('The editor used a semicolon to join two clauses, but typed a question mark instead of the mark ;.','The editor used a semicolon (;) to join the closely related clauses.','问号与分号是不同标点；分号的符号是 ;。','meaning'),[q('Which mark joined the clauses?','a semicolon','a comma only','a question mark','编辑用分号连接了两个分句。',1,'context'),q('Could the second clause stand alone?','yes, it could be a sentence','no, it was only a fragment','only if it became a heading','第二个分句可以独立成句。',1,'context'),q('Which symbol is a semicolon?',';','?','!','分号的符号是 ;。',1,'meaning'),q('How does a semicolon compare with a comma and a full stop?','stronger than a comma but weaker than a full stop','weaker than a comma and stronger than a full stop','identical in force to a question mark','分号的停顿力度强于逗号而弱于句号。',1,'meaning')]);
P('semiconductor','Semiconductor combines semi- and conductor; it names a material with electrical conductivity between that of an insulator and a conductor, or a device made from it.',[C('semiconductor.s1','半导体材料','Silicon is a semiconductor used to control current in electronic circuits.','硅是一种用于控制电子电路中电流的半导体。','Silicon is a semiconductor / used to control current / in electronic circuits.','semiconductor.s1 指导电能力介于绝缘体与导体之间的固体材料。','硅材料可控制电流。'),C('semiconductor.s2','半导体器件；芯片','The technician replaced a damaged semiconductor in the phone’s power-control module.','技术员更换了手机电源控制模块中损坏的半导体器件。','The technician replaced a semiconductor / in the phone’s / power-control module.','semiconductor.s2 也可指由半导体材料制成的电子元件。','器件位于手机电源模块。')],M('Silicon is a semiconductor because it conducts electricity better than copper and is a perfect insulator.','Silicon is a semiconductor because its conductivity is between that of an insulator and a metal.','金属导电能力比硅更强；半导体并非完美绝缘体。','meaning'),[q('What material is used to control current in the circuit?','silicon','rubber','wood','硅半导体用于控制电路电流。',1,'context'),q('What did the technician replace in the phone?','a damaged semiconductor device','the entire phone screen','a paper label','技术员更换了电源控制模块中的半导体器件。',2,'context'),q('What is a semiconductor material?','a material with conductivity between an insulator and a conductor','a material that never conducts any electricity','a metal that conducts better than copper','semiconductor 材料的导电能力介于绝缘体与导体之间。',1,'meaning'),q('What can semiconductor also name?','an electronic component made from semiconductor material','only a person who sells phones','a tool for measuring temperature','semiconductor 也可指由该类材料制成的电子器件。',2,'meaning')]);
P('semiliterate','Semiliterate combines semi- (“partly”) and literate; it describes someone with only a partial ability to read and write.',C('semiliterate.s1','识字不多的人','The adult-education tutor adapted the form because one applicant was semiliterate and struggled with long written instructions.','一名申请者识字不多，难以理解冗长书面说明，因此成人教育辅导员调整了表格。','The tutor adapted the form / because the applicant was semiliterate / and struggled with long instructions.','semiliterate.s1 指读写能力有限、只能部分识字的人。','冗长书面说明对申请者有困难。'),M('The applicant was semiliterate and easily read the complex legal form without help.','The applicant was semiliterate and struggled to read the complex form.','若能轻松阅读复杂表格，就不符合读写能力有限这一描述。','meaning'),[q('Why did the tutor adapt the form?','the applicant struggled with long written instructions','the form contained no words','the applicant wrote the form for the tutor','申请者难以理解冗长书面说明，辅导员因此调整了表格。',1,'context'),q('What type of class was the tutor supporting?','adult education','a semiconductor design lab','a university senate meeting','辅导员在成人教育项目中帮助申请者。',1,'context'),q('What does semiliterate describe?','having only a partial ability to read and write','being unable to speak any language','being fluent in several written languages','semiliterate 指读写能力有限。',1,'meaning'),q('Which description fits a semiliterate person?','someone who can read simple notices but struggles with complex forms','someone who edits long legal documents professionally','someone who cannot hear spoken instructions','能读简单通知但难读复杂表格的人可称为 semiliterate。',1,'context')]);
P('semimolten','Semimolten combines semi- (“partly”) and molten, the past participle of melt; it means heated until partly, but not completely, liquid.',C('semimolten.s1','部分熔融的','The glassmaker shaped the semimolten glass while its center was soft and its outer layer had begun to cool.','玻璃工趁半熔融的玻璃中心柔软、外层开始冷却时进行塑形。','The glassmaker shaped semimolten glass / while its center stayed soft / and the outside cooled.','semimolten.s1 指受热后部分变成液体、但尚未完全熔化。','材料一部分柔软，外层已冷却。'),M('The glass was semimolten after it had cooled completely into a hard, solid block.','The glass was semimolten while part of it remained soft and partly liquid.','完全冷却凝固的玻璃已不处于部分熔融状态。','meaning'),[q('When did the glassmaker shape the glass?','while its center was soft and the outside began to cool','after the glass had become completely cold','before the glass was heated at all','玻璃工在玻璃中心仍柔软、外层开始冷却时塑形。',1,'context'),q('Was the glass completely liquid?','no, it was only partly molten','yes, every part had become liquid','no, it had never been heated','玻璃只是部分熔融，并未完全液化。',1,'context'),q('What does semimolten mean?','partly, but not completely, melted','frozen solid','heated without any change','semimolten 指部分而非完全熔化。',1,'meaning'),q('Which material is semimolten?','wax with a soft liquid center and a still-solid edge','metal cooled into a hard block','ice that has never warmed','中心柔软、边缘仍为固体的蜡是 semimolten。',1,'context')]);
P('seminar','Seminar comes through German Seminar from Latin seminarium (“seed plot”); it can be a small-group class or a meeting for discussion or training.',[C('seminar.s1','研讨班；讨论课','In the seminar, eight students discussed two competing interpretations of the poem with their instructor.','在研讨课上，八名学生与教师讨论了这首诗的两种不同解读。','In the seminar, eight students discussed / two interpretations / with their instructor.','seminar.s1 指由小组围绕某个主题讨论的课程。','学生在小班课堂中讨论诗歌。'),C('seminar.s2','研讨会','The hospital held a one-day seminar on emergency response for nurses from nearby clinics.','医院为附近诊所的护士举办了一天的急救响应研讨会。','The hospital held a one-day seminar / on emergency response / for nearby nurses.','seminar.s2 指用于培训或讨论的会议。','研讨会面向附近诊所护士。')],M('The hospital’s seminar on emergency response was a private one-person exam with no discussion or training.','The hospital held a seminar to discuss and train nurses in emergency response.','seminar 是讨论或培训活动，不是独自参加的考试。','meaning'),[q('How many students discussed the poem in class?','eight','eighty','two instructors only','研讨课上有八名学生讨论诗歌。',1,'context'),q('Who attended the hospital seminar?','nurses from nearby clinics','the poem’s publisher','semiconductor technicians only','医院为附近诊所的护士举办研讨会。',2,'context'),q('What is a seminar in the classroom example?','a small-group class for discussion','an individual written exam','a university governing council','第一句 seminar 指小组讨论课。',1,'meaning'),q('What is a seminar in the hospital example?','a meeting for training or discussion','a six-month academic term','a device made from silicon','医院句中的 seminar 指培训或讨论会议。',2,'meaning')]);
P('semiotics','Semiotics comes from Greek sēmeiōtikos (“of signs”), from sēmeion (“sign”); it is the theory or study of signs in language, images, and culture.',C('semiotics.s1','符号论','Her semiotics project compared how a red flag communicates danger in road signs, films, and public demonstrations.','她的符号论项目比较红旗在道路标志、电影和公众示威中如何传达危险。','Her semiotics project compared a red flag / across road signs, films / and demonstrations.','semiotics.s1 指研究语言、图像和文化符号的理论。','项目探讨同一符号在不同场景中的意义。'),M('The project was semiotics because it measured only the flag’s weight and ignored every sign or meaning.','The project was semiotics because it studied how a flag communicates meaning in different settings.','只测重量而不研究符号意义，不属于符号论研究。','meaning'),[q('Which symbol did the project compare?','a red flag','a semicolon','a silicon chip','项目比较的是红旗。',1,'context'),q('Where did it examine the flag’s meaning?','in road signs, films, and demonstrations','only in a chemistry lab','only in a university budget','项目比较红旗在道路标志、电影和示威中的意义。',1,'context'),q('What is semiotics?','the study or theory of signs and how they communicate meaning','the study of six-month school terms','the manufacture of electronic chips','semiotics 指研究符号及其意义的理论。',1,'meaning'),q('Which investigation belongs to semiotics?','studying how a logo signals trust in different cultures','measuring the conductivity of silicon','counting how many students attend a seminar','研究标志如何在不同文化中传达信任属于 semiotics。',1,'context')]);
P('semiskilled','Semiskilled combines semi- (“partly”) and skilled; it describes a worker or job requiring limited training rather than advanced expertise.',C('semiskilled.s1','只需部分技能的','The factory hired semiskilled workers to package parts after a short safety and equipment course.','工厂聘用只需部分技能的工人，他们完成简短的安全与设备课程后负责包装零件。','The factory hired semiskilled workers / after a short course / to package parts.','semiskilled.s1 描述只需有限培训或部分技能即可胜任的工作或工人。','工人经简短培训即可完成包装工作。'),M('The semiskilled job required years of specialist surgery training and a medical degree.','The semiskilled job required only a short safety and equipment course.','多年专科手术培训超出了有限技能工作所需。','meaning'),[q('What did the factory workers package?','parts','seminar handouts','legal contracts','工人负责包装零件。',1,'context'),q('What training did they receive?','a short safety and equipment course','years of specialist surgery training','no introduction to safety','他们完成了简短的安全与设备课程。',1,'context'),q('What does semiskilled mean?','requiring only limited training or skill','requiring the highest level of professional expertise','requiring no work at all','semiskilled 指只需有限培训或技能。',1,'meaning'),q('Which role is semiskilled?','packing parts after a brief equipment course','performing complex surgery after years of medical school','designing a new semiconductor from scratch','简短设备培训后包装零件的工作属于 semiskilled。',1,'context')]);
P('senate','Senate comes from Latin senatus, from senex (“old”); it can mean a parliament’s upper house or a governing council at some universities.',[C('senate.s1','参议院；上院','The senate voted on the transport bill after hearing arguments from both the government and opposition.','听取政府和反对派的意见后，参议院就交通法案进行表决。','The senate voted on the bill / after hearing arguments / from both sides.','senate.s1 指某些国家议会中的上院。','议员听取双方意见后表决。'),C('senate.s2','大学评议会','The university senate approved a new policy for research ethics and graduate supervision.','大学评议会批准了新的研究伦理与研究生指导政策。','The university senate approved a policy / for research ethics / and graduate supervision.','senate.s2 指某些大学负责治理事务的委员会。','大学治理机构批准政策。')],M('The university senate was a group of high-school athletes elected to score goals in a match.','The university senate was a governing council that approved academic policies.','大学评议会负责治理而非参加体育比赛。','meaning'),[q('What did the parliamentary senate vote on?','the transport bill','a graduate thesis title','a semiconductor label','参议院就交通法案进行了表决。',1,'context'),q('What policy did the university senate approve?','one on research ethics and graduate supervision','one setting the price of a signed novel','one replacing every academic course with sport','大学评议会批准了研究伦理和研究生指导政策。',2,'context'),q('What is a senate in the first example?','the upper house of a parliament','a small discussion class','a company that sells abroad','第一句 senate 指议会的上院。',1,'meaning'),q('What can senate mean at a university?','a governing council','a student who attends the final year','an individual course term','senate 在一些大学里可指治理评议会。',2,'meaning')]);
P('senator','Senator comes from Latin senator, a member of a senatus (“council of elders”); it means an elected or appointed member of a senate.',C('senator.s1','上院议员','The senator questioned the minister about the cost of the flood barriers before voting on the bill.','这名上院议员在就法案投票前，质询部长防洪屏障的费用。','The senator questioned the minister / about the flood barriers / before voting.','senator.s1 指参议院或其他上院的选举或任命成员。','议员就公共法案质询部长。'),M('The senator was a laboratory material that controlled current in the flood barrier.','The senator was a member of the senate who questioned the minister.','senator 指议会成员，不是半导体材料。','meaning'),[q('What did the senator ask the minister about?','the cost of flood barriers','the price of a cookbook','the meaning of a semicolon','议员询问了防洪屏障的费用。',1,'context'),q('What was the senator preparing to do?','vote on the bill','sell the barriers abroad','teach a small-group seminar','议员随后准备就法案投票。',1,'context'),q('What is a senator?','a member of a senate','a material with partial conductivity','a university term lasting six months','senator 指参议院或上院成员。',1,'meaning'),q('Who is a senator?','an elected upper-house member debating legislation','a seller offering furniture at an auction','a student in a spring semester','参与立法辩论的上院民选成员是 senator。',1,'context')]);
P('send','Send comes from Old English sendan (“cause to go, dispatch”); it can mean arrange for a person or thing to go somewhere or cause someone to enter a state.',[C('send.s1','寄；发送；派遣','The clinic sent the test results to the patient through its secure online portal.','诊所通过安全的在线门户把检测结果发送给患者。','The clinic sent the test results / to the patient / through a secure portal.','send.s1 指安排某人或某物前往某处。','诊所把结果发给患者。'),C('send.s2','使处于某种状态','The unexpected final score sent the visiting supporters into a burst of celebration.','意外的终场比分让客队球迷顿时欢庆起来。','The unexpected score sent the supporters / into a burst / of celebration.','send.s2 可指使某人进入某种状态或情绪。','比分使球迷进入欢庆状态。')],M('The clinic sent the results to the patient by keeping them in its own computer and never delivering them.','The clinic sent the results to the patient through its secure portal.','结果若未交付给患者，就没有发送给患者。','meaning'),[q('How did the clinic send the test results?','through a secure online portal','by announcing them at a stadium','by storing them without telling the patient','诊所通过安全的在线门户发送检测结果。',1,'context'),q('What did the unexpected score cause the supporters to do?','burst into celebration','leave the stadium before the match','send a medical sample','比分让客队球迷欢庆起来。',2,'context'),q('What does send mean in the clinic example?','to arrange for something to go to someone','to keep something permanently in one place','to criticize a person angrily','诊所句中的 send 指把结果发给患者。',1,'meaning'),q('What does send mean in “sent the supporters into celebration”?','caused them to enter an emotional state','mailed them a paper ticket','asked them to leave the team','该句中的 send 指使球迷进入欢庆状态。',2,'meaning')]);
P('send for','Send for combines send and for; it means ask someone to come, often in an emergency, or order goods to be delivered.',[C('send for.s1','派人去请；召唤','When the hiker’s ankle swelled, the guide sent for a medic from the nearest station.','徒步者的脚踝肿起来后，向导派人去最近的站点请医护人员。','The guide sent for a medic / when the hiker’s ankle / began to swell.','send for.s1 指要求某人来到自己所在的地方，常用于紧急情况。','向导召来医护人员。'),C('send for.s2','函购；订购','Unable to find the map locally, Nora sent for a copy from the publisher by mail.','诺拉在当地找不到那张地图，便向出版社邮购了一份。','Nora sent for a copy / from the publisher / by mail.','send for.s2 指订购商品并要求寄送给自己。','她通过邮寄订购地图。')],M('The guide sent for a medic by telling the injured hiker to travel alone and not calling anyone.','The guide sent for a medic to come help the injured hiker.','不通知或召请任何人不符合 send for。','meaning'),[q('Why did the guide send for a medic?','the hiker’s ankle had swollen','the map had arrived','the seminar needed a speaker','徒步者脚踝肿胀，向导因此召请医护人员。',1,'context'),q('How did Nora obtain the map?','she ordered a copy from the publisher by mail','she asked a medic to bring it','she found it in the local shop','诺拉从出版社邮购了一份地图。',2,'context'),q('What does send for mean in the hiking example?','ask someone to come to where help is needed','mail an item to another address','send someone away from a meeting','徒步句中的 send for 指请医护人员赶来。',1,'meaning'),q('What does send for mean in the map example?','order goods to be delivered','ask the map to come to a clinic','refuse to buy an item','邮购句中的 send for 指订购并要求寄送。',2,'meaning')]);
P('send off','Send off combines send and off; it means dispatch a letter, parcel, or form, or order a player to leave a game as punishment.',[C('send off.s1','寄出；发出','She sent off the signed application by registered post before the scholarship deadline.','她在奖学金截止日期前用挂号信寄出了签字申请表。','She sent off the application / by registered post / before the deadline.','send off.s1 指把信件、包裹或表格寄给个人或机构。','申请表通过邮政寄出。'),C('send off.s2','（体育）罚下场','The referee sent off the defender after a dangerous tackle in the final minutes.','最后几分钟中，裁判因一次危险铲球将后卫罚下场。','The referee sent off the defender / after a dangerous tackle / late in the game.','send off.s2 指比赛中作为处罚命令球员离场。','球员因危险犯规被罚下。')],M('The referee sent off the defender by awarding him a medal and ordering him to remain on the field.','The referee sent off the defender by ordering him to leave the field as a punishment.','颁奖并要求留场与罚下场相反。','meaning'),[q('How did she send off the application?','by registered post','by asking the referee to carry it','by leaving it unsigned at home','她用挂号信寄出申请表。',1,'context'),q('Why was the defender sent off?','he made a dangerous tackle','he mailed an application','he scored a winning goal','后卫因危险铲球被罚下。',2,'context'),q('What does send off mean for the application?','dispatch it to an organization','ask someone to arrive at an emergency','reject it after reviewing it','send off 在申请表句中指寄出。',1,'meaning'),q('What does send off mean in the match?','order a player to leave as punishment','send the player a letter','invite the player onto the field','比赛中的 send off 指因处罚命令球员离场。',2,'meaning')]);
P('send on','Send on combines send and on; it means forward a letter, message, or parcel to another person after receiving it.',C('send on.s1','转寄；转发','After moving offices, Daniel asked reception to send on any letters that still arrived at his old address.','丹尼尔搬办公室后，请前台把仍寄到旧地址的信件转寄给他。','Daniel asked reception to send on letters / that reached / his old address.','send on.s1 指收到信件、消息或包裹后再转交给别人。','前台把旧地址收到的信转寄给他。'),M('Reception sent on Daniel’s letters by opening them and throwing them away instead of forwarding them.','Reception sent on Daniel’s letters by forwarding them to his new office.','销毁信件而不是转寄，不符合 send on。','meaning'),[q('Where did some of Daniel’s letters still arrive?','at his old address','at the hospital station','at the publisher’s foreign office','有些信件仍寄到丹尼尔的旧地址。',1,'context'),q('What did he ask reception to do?','forward those letters to his new office','send the letters to the referee','sell the letters at auction','丹尼尔请前台把信件转寄到新办公室。',1,'context'),q('What does send on mean?','forward something received to another person','send an original parcel abroad before it arrives','ask someone to come in an emergency','send on 指收到后再转寄或转发。',1,'meaning'),q('Which action is sending on?','forwarding a message to its intended recipient after it reaches you','writing and mailing a new message yourself','deleting a message without passing it along','收到消息后转发给收件人属于 send on。',1,'context')]);
P('send-off','Send-off combines send and off as a noun; it means a gathering to wish someone well when leaving, or in sport the act of expelling a player.',[C('send-off.s1','欢送会；送行','Coworkers organized a warm send-off for Amira on her last day at the research center.','阿米拉在研究中心的最后一天，同事们为她举办了温馨的欢送会。','Coworkers organized a send-off / for Amira / on her last day.','send-off.s1 指为即将离职、离队或离开某地的人送行的聚会。','同事们为她举办送别聚会。'),C('send-off.s2','（体育）罚下场','The captain’s send-off left the team with ten players after he received a second yellow card.','队长吃到第二张黄牌被罚下后，球队只剩十名球员。','The captain’s send-off left the team / with ten players / after a second yellow card.','send-off.s2 在体育比赛中指罚令球员离场的行为。','队长被罚下，球队少一人。')],M('The coworkers held a send-off for Amira by welcoming her to her first day at the center.','The coworkers held a send-off for Amira as she left the research center.','送行聚会为离开者举行，而不是欢迎新人入职。','meaning'),[q('When was Amira’s send-off held?','on her last day at the research center','on the first day of her new job','during the team’s match','同事们在阿米拉离开研究中心的最后一天为她送行。',1,'context'),q('Why did the team have only ten players?','the captain received a second yellow card and was expelled','coworkers held a farewell party','the captain scored twice','队长因第二张黄牌被罚下，球队只剩十人。',2,'context'),q('What is a send-off in the research-center example?','a gathering to wish a departing person well','a disciplinary order in a match','an application sent by mail','研究中心句中的 send-off 指欢送会。',1,'meaning'),q('What is a send-off in the sports example?','the expulsion of a player from the game','a party held when a player retires','a goal scored at the final whistle','体育句中的 send-off 指罚下场。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sender','Sender is formed from send and -er; it means the person or machine from which a message begins.',C('sender.s1','发件人；发送端','The email sender used the return address shown in the message header to receive the reply.','电子邮件发件人使用邮件标题中显示的回信地址接收回复。','The email sender used the return address / shown in the header / to receive a reply.','sender.s1 指消息的来源者或发送设备。','邮件标题标明发件人地址。'),M('The sender was the person who received the email but did not create or transmit it.','The sender was the person who sent the email.','接收邮件的人是收件人，不是 sender。','meaning'),[q('Where was the sender’s return address shown?','in the message header','on the referee’s card','inside the semiconductor','发件人的回信地址显示在邮件标题中。',1,'context'),q('Why did the sender use that address?','to receive the reply','to send off a football player','to mark the start of a semester','发件人用该地址接收回复。',1,'context'),q('What does sender mean?','the person or machine from which a message starts','the person who receives a message only','a person who forwards every letter','sender 指消息的发送者或发送设备。',1,'meaning'),q('Who is the sender of an email?','the account that transmitted it','the account that only opened it','the person named in its attachment','发送邮件的账户是 sender。',1,'context')]);
P('senescent','Senescent comes from Latin senescere (“to grow old”), from senex (“old”); it describes a cell, organ, or organism becoming aged.',C('senescent.s1','老化中的','Researchers tracked senescent cells in the tissue sample to learn how aging changed their repair activity.','研究人员追踪组织样本中的衰老细胞，以了解老化如何改变其修复活动。','Researchers tracked senescent cells / to learn how aging changed / their repair activity.','senescent.s1 指细胞、器官或生物体正在变老。','研究关注衰老细胞的修复能力。'),M('The sample contained senescent cells that were newly formed and showed no signs of aging.','The sample contained senescent cells that were aging and had altered repair activity.','新形成且无衰老迹象的细胞不是 senescent。','meaning'),[q('What did researchers track?','senescent cells in a tissue sample','semicircular seats in a hall','a senator’s email sender','研究人员追踪组织样本中的衰老细胞。',1,'context'),q('What activity did aging change?','the cells’ repair activity','the number of semester weeks','the price of the sample','研究考察老化如何改变细胞修复活动。',1,'context'),q('What does senescent mean?','becoming aged, especially of a cell or organism','newly created and rapidly growing','unable to conduct electricity','senescent 指正在老化的。',1,'meaning'),q('Which cell is senescent?','an aging cell whose repair function has changed','a newly formed cell with no aging signs','a silicon particle in a circuit','修复功能随老化改变的细胞可称为 senescent。',1,'context')]);
P('senile','Senile comes from Latin senilis, from senex (“old”); it describes mental or physical weakening associated with advanced age.',C('senile.s1','年老衰弱的；年老糊涂的','The doctor avoided calling a patient senile without assessment and instead described the specific memory changes.','医生没有未经评估就称患者年老糊涂，而是具体说明了记忆变化。','The doctor avoided calling the patient senile / without assessment / and described specific changes.','senile.s1 指因高龄而出现的身心衰弱，使用时应谨慎，避免笼统贴标签。','医生改用具体描述，避免轻率诊断。'),M('The doctor diagnosed the patient as senile solely because he was elderly, without examining his memory or health.','The doctor assessed the patient’s memory and health before describing age-related impairment.','不能仅凭年龄作诊断；应先评估具体症状。','meaning'),[q('What did the doctor describe instead of applying a label?','the patient’s specific memory changes','the patient’s email address','the patient’s semester schedule','医生具体说明了患者的记忆变化。',1,'context'),q('What did the doctor avoid doing?','calling the patient senile without an assessment','examining the patient’s health','explaining observed symptoms','医生避免未经评估就称患者 senile。',1,'context'),q('What does senile describe in the source sense?','mental or physical weakening linked with advanced age','a person who is simply older than another','a person who sends a message','senile 指与高龄相关的身心衰弱。',1,'meaning'),q('Why should the word senile be used carefully?','it can label age-related impairment without describing specific evidence','it always means a person is young','it names a university governing council','senile 若不结合具体证据，可能只是笼统给人贴上衰老标签。',1,'meaning')]);
P('senior','Senior comes from Latin senior (“older”), the comparative of senex (“old”); it can mean older, higher in rank, or an older person or final-year student.',[C('senior.s1','年长的；资历较老的','Rina is senior to Mark by three years, although they joined the department on the same day.','莉娜比马克年长三岁，尽管他们同一天加入部门。','Rina is senior to Mark / by three years / though they joined together.','senior.s1 指年龄或资历比另一人更大的。','莉娜年长三岁。'),C('senior.s2','高级的；级别高的','A senior engineer reviewed the design and approved the junior team’s safety calculations.','一名高级工程师审查设计，并批准了初级团队的安全计算。','A senior engineer reviewed the design / and approved / the team’s calculations.','senior.s2 指职位或级别较高的。','高级工程师审核工作。'),C('senior.s3','高年级学生；年长者；上司','Every high-school senior submitted a graduation plan before the final semester began.','每名高中毕业年级学生都在最后一学期开始前提交了毕业计划。','Every high-school senior submitted a plan / before the final semester / began.','senior.s3 可作名词，指年长者、高年级学生或上司。','高中毕业年级学生提交计划。')],M('The junior engineer was senior to the director because the junior title always ranks above director.','The director was senior to the junior engineer because the director held a higher rank.','junior 职位低于 director；职位级别高低不能颠倒。','meaning'),[q('How many years older is Rina than Mark?','three','one','ten','莉娜比马克年长三岁。',1,'context'),q('What did the senior engineer approve?','the junior team’s safety calculations','a student’s cookbook','the school’s selling prices','高级工程师批准了初级团队的安全计算。',2,'context'),q('What does senior mean in “senior engineer”?','higher in rank','younger in age','a final-year high-school student','senior engineer 中 senior 表示职位级别较高。',2,'meaning'),q('Who is a high-school senior in the third example?','a student in the final year of high school','a first-year primary pupil','a person who sells goods abroad','高中 senior 指毕业年级学生。',3,'meaning')]);
P('seniority','Seniority is formed from senior and -ity; it means higher rank based on age or length of service.',C('seniority.s1','资历；年资','Promotion followed seniority at the company, so employees with longer service were considered first.','公司按资历晋升，因此工龄较长的员工会优先考虑。','Promotion followed seniority / so employees with longer service / were considered first.','seniority.s1 指按年龄或服务年限取得的较高资历或级别。','较长工龄决定考虑顺序。'),M('The company awarded seniority to the newest employee solely because that person had worked there for one week.','The company awarded seniority to employees with longer service.','仅工作一周的新员工并无更长服务年限。','meaning'),[q('Whom did the company consider first for promotion?','employees with longer service','employees who had just started','customers with the newest receipts','公司优先考虑工龄较长的员工。',1,'context'),q('What determined the promotion order?','seniority','the price of the company’s products','the shape of the meeting room','晋升顺序按资历决定。',1,'context'),q('What does seniority mean?','higher rank based on age or length of service','a person’s ability to sell abroad','a class held during one semester','seniority 指按年龄或服务年限形成的资历。',1,'meaning'),q('Which rule uses seniority?','promoting the employee with the longest service first','promoting the newest hire first regardless of experience','choosing by lottery only','优先晋升工龄最长的员工体现 seniority。',1,'context')]);
P('sensation','Sensation comes from Latin sensatio, from sentire (“feel”); it can mean a physical feeling or great excitement/a person or event that causes it.',[C('sensation.s1','感觉；知觉','A tingling sensation in her fingers began after she held the cold railing for several minutes.','她握着冰冷栏杆几分钟后，手指出现了刺痛感。','A tingling sensation began / in her fingers / after holding the cold railing.','sensation.s1 指身体感受到的感觉。','手指产生刺痛这一身体感觉。'),C('sensation.s2','轰动；引起轰动的人或事','The rookie became a sensation after scoring three goals in her first international match.','这名新秀在首场国际比赛中攻入三球后，一举引起轰动。','The rookie became a sensation / after scoring three goals / in her first international match.','sensation.s2 指引起强烈兴奋或关注的人、事件或现象。','球员的表现引起广泛关注。')],M('A tingling sensation in her fingers was a public event that excited an entire country.','A tingling sensation was a physical feeling in her fingers.','手指的刺痛是身体感觉，不是引起公众轰动的事件。','meaning'),[q('What caused the tingling sensation?','holding the cold railing for several minutes','scoring three goals','sending off a defender','她握着冰冷栏杆后手指出现刺痛感。',1,'context'),q('Why did the rookie become a sensation?','she scored three goals in her first international match','she held a cold railing','she was appointed to the senate','新秀首场国际比赛攻入三球，因此引起轰动。',2,'context'),q('What does sensation mean in the first example?','a physical feeling','a political upper house','a high rank earned through service','第一句 sensation 指身体感觉。',1,'meaning'),q('What is a sensation in the sports example?','a person or event causing great excitement','a mild feeling in one finger','a message sender','体育句中的 sensation 指引起轰动的人。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sensational','Sensational is formed from sensation and -al; it means causing intense public interest, shock, or excitement, or wonderful in informal use.',[C('sensational.s1','轰动的；耸人听闻的','The newspaper ran a sensational headline about the rescue, though its story contained no evidence for the dramatic claim.','报纸刊登了一条关于救援的耸人听闻标题，尽管报道没有证据支持其戏剧化说法。','The newspaper ran a sensational headline / though the story offered / no supporting evidence.','sensational.s1 指引起公众强烈兴趣、震惊或兴奋的，也可带有夸张意味。','标题夸大救援消息以吸引关注。'),C('sensational.s2','极好的；精彩的','The pianist gave a sensational performance, and the audience stood to applaud at the end.','钢琴家奉献了一场精彩绝伦的演出，结束时观众起立鼓掌。','The pianist gave a sensational performance / and the audience / stood to applaud.','sensational.s2 在非正式褒义用法中表示极好、精彩。','观众起立鼓掌表示赞赏。')],M('The newspaper published a sensational headline that was quiet, ordinary, and attracted no public attention.','The newspaper published a sensational headline designed to attract intense public attention.','平淡且无人注意的标题不具轰动性。','meaning'),[q('What was missing from the newspaper’s dramatic claim?','evidence','a pianist','a concert hall','报道没有证据支持耸人听闻的说法。',1,'context'),q('How did the audience respond to the pianist?','they stood to applaud','they sent the performer off the field','they left before the music began','观众在演出结束时起立鼓掌。',2,'context'),q('What does sensational mean in the headline example?','causing intense public interest or shock','ordinary and unnoticed','based on a physical tingling feeling','标题句中的 sensational 指引起公众强烈关注或震惊。',1,'meaning'),q('What does sensational mean in the concert example?','wonderful and very impressive','scandalous but unsupported','merely related to the senses','演出句中的 sensational 是“精彩绝伦”的褒义表达。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sensationalism','Sensationalism is formed from sensational and -ism; it means using shocking or exaggerated material to attract attention.',C('sensationalism.s1','耸人听闻；哗众取宠','The channel’s sensationalism was clear when it used a frightening headline unsupported by the verified report.','这家频道用未经核实的可怕标题吸引眼球，其耸人听闻的做法显而易见。','The channel’s sensationalism was clear / when it used a frightening headline / unsupported by the report.','sensationalism.s1 指为吸引注意而使用震惊或夸张内容的做法。','标题夸大事实以获取关注。'),M('The channel showed sensationalism by reporting the verified facts plainly without exaggeration or shock tactics.','The channel showed sensationalism by using a shocking unsupported headline to attract attention.','平实报道核实事实而不夸大，不属于哗众取宠。','meaning'),[q('What did the channel use to attract attention?','a frightening headline unsupported by the verified report','a plain correction of its earlier story','a list of semester dates','频道使用了未经核实的可怕标题吸引眼球。',1,'context'),q('What was unsupported?','the frightening headline','the verified report','the correction of a spelling error','可怕的标题缺少已核实报道的支持。',1,'context'),q('What does sensationalism mean?','using shocking or exaggerated material to attract attention','reporting evidence plainly without exaggeration','a feeling caused by a physical stimulus','sensationalism 指用震惊或夸张内容吸引注意。',1,'meaning'),q('Which report displays sensationalism?','one that exaggerates an unverified danger to win attention','one that carefully corrects a false headline','one that states verified results without drama','夸大未经核实的危险以吸引关注，体现 sensationalism。',1,'context')]);
P('sense','Sense comes from Old French sens and Latin sensus (“feeling, perception”); it can mean a physical faculty or feeling, a word’s meaning, or becoming aware of something.',[C('sense.s1','感官；感觉','The sharp sense of smell helped the rescue dog locate a child beneath the fallen tent.','敏锐的嗅觉帮助搜救犬找到倒塌帐篷下的孩子。','The sharp sense of smell / helped the rescue dog / locate a child.','sense.s1 指五种身体感官之一或身体感受到的感觉。','嗅觉帮助搜救犬发现气味。'),C('sense.s2','意义；意思','In the sentence “The lights went out,” the word “out” has the sense of “not lit.”','在“The lights went out”这句话里，out 的意思是“没有亮”。','The word “out” has the sense / of “not lit” / in this sentence.','sense.s2 指词语或情境所表达的含义。','例句解释了 out 的一个词义。'),C('sense.s3','察觉；意识到','Mara sensed that the room had grown quiet when everyone stopped talking at once.','大家突然都不说话时，玛拉察觉到房间安静了下来。','Mara sensed that the room was quiet / when everyone / stopped talking.','sense.s3 作动词，指未被告知而察觉到某事。','玛拉从环境变化中察觉到安静。')],M('Mara sensed the room was quiet by reading a written announcement that explicitly told her so.','Mara sensed the room was quiet when everyone suddenly stopped talking.','直接读到明确通知是被告知，不是凭迹象察觉。','meaning'),[q('Which ability helped the rescue dog find the child?','its sense of smell','its sense of grammar','its sense of balance only','搜救犬靠敏锐的嗅觉找到孩子。',1,'context'),q('What does “out” mean in the lights sentence?','not lit','outside the building','very loud','例句中 out 表示灯没有亮。',2,'context'),q('What does sense mean in “Mara sensed the room was quiet”?','become aware of something without being told','the exact definition of a word','one of the five body organs','玛拉句中的 sensed 指未被告知而察觉。',3,'meaning'),q('What does “a sense of smell” refer to?','a physical faculty for detecting odors','the opinion that a plan is fair','a complete sentence','sense of smell 指辨别气味的身体感官。',1,'meaning')]);
P('senseless','Senseless combines sense and -less; it can mean without meaning or good reason, or unconscious after injury, shock, or drugs.',[C('senseless.s1','无意义的；毫无道理的','The senseless delay left the bridge closed for hours even though the inspection had already cleared it.','毫无道理的延误让桥封闭了几个小时，尽管检查早已通过。','The senseless delay kept the bridge closed / even though the inspection / had cleared it.','senseless.s1 指没有意义、目的或合理理由的。','检查已通过，继续封桥没有理由。'),C('senseless.s2','失去知觉的；不省人事的','The cyclist was senseless for several minutes after the fall, so a bystander called emergency services.','骑车人摔倒后有几分钟失去知觉，一名路人因此拨打了急救电话。','The cyclist was senseless for minutes / after the fall / so help was called.','senseless.s2 指因撞击、休克或药物而失去意识。','摔倒后骑车人短暂昏迷。')],M('The cyclist was senseless after the fall but remained fully awake, speaking clearly throughout.','The cyclist was senseless after the fall and had lost consciousness.','完全清醒且能清晰说话与失去知觉相矛盾。','meaning'),[q('Why was the bridge delay called senseless?','the inspection had already cleared it','the bridge had failed inspection','the delay protected workers from a hazard','检查已通过，继续封桥没有合理理由。',1,'context'),q('What happened to the cyclist after the fall?','the cyclist lost consciousness for several minutes','the cyclist immediately rode home','the cyclist inspected the bridge','骑车人摔倒后短暂失去知觉。',2,'context'),q('What does senseless mean in the bridge example?','without a good reason or purpose','unable to feel after an injury','full of careful reasoning','此处 senseless 指毫无合理理由的。',1,'meaning'),q('What does senseless mean about the cyclist?','unconscious','unpopular','unreasonable but fully awake','描述骑车人时，senseless 指失去知觉。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sensibility','Sensibility comes from French sensibilité and Latin sensibilis (“perceptible”); it means a capacity for delicate feeling or a particular way of responding.',C('sensibility.s1','感性；敏感的鉴赏力','Her artistic sensibility led her to notice the quiet contrast between the pale wall and the blue ceramic bowl.','她的艺术感受力使她注意到浅色墙壁与蓝色陶碗之间微妙的对比。','Her artistic sensibility led her to notice / the quiet contrast / between wall and bowl.','sensibility.s1 指细腻感受或形成特定反应方式的能力。','她察觉到不显眼的色彩对比。'),M('Her artistic sensibility prevented her from noticing the subtle contrast between the wall and the bowl.','Her artistic sensibility helped her notice the subtle contrast.','善于感受细节使她注意到差别，并非视而不见。','meaning'),[q('What contrast did her sensibility help her notice?','the pale wall and blue ceramic bowl','two identical blue bowls','the bridge inspection times','她注意到浅墙与蓝色陶碗之间的对比。',1,'context'),q('What quality does the example emphasize?','attention to subtle artistic details','ability to sell products abroad','loss of consciousness','例句强调她对细微艺术细节的感受力。',1,'context'),q('What is sensibility?','a capacity for delicate feeling or response','the absence of all physical senses','a device that measures movement','sensibility 指细腻感受或回应的能力。',1,'meaning'),q('Who shows artistic sensibility?','someone who notices a subtle color contrast','someone who ignores every visual detail','someone who cannot see any colors','能注意到细微色彩对比的人体现艺术感受力。',1,'context')]);
P('sensible','Sensible comes from Latin sensibilis (“perceptible”); it can mean reasonable in judgment, practical and likely to work, or plain and comfortable clothing.',[C('sensible.s1','明智的；有判断力的','It was sensible of Jo to check the storm warning before taking the boat onto the lake.','乔上船去湖上之前先查看风暴预警，这样做很明智。','It was sensible of Jo / to check the warning / before taking the boat out.','sensible.s1 指能冷静判断、采取合理行动的。','出船前查看预警是合理判断。'),C('sensible.s2','合理的；切实可行的','A sensible repair plan uses available parts and can be finished before the factory reopens.','合理的维修方案使用现有零件，并能在工厂重新开工前完成。','A sensible repair plan uses available parts / and can be finished / before reopening.','sensible.s2 指依据事实、切实可行而可能成功的。','方案能用现有资源及时完成。'),C('sensible.s3','（衣着、鞋）朴素实用的','For the rocky trail, Lina wore sensible shoes with firm soles instead of delicate high heels.','走岩石小径时，莉娜穿了鞋底结实的实用鞋，而不是精致的高跟鞋。','Lina wore sensible shoes / with firm soles / on the rocky trail.','sensible.s3 形容衣鞋时指朴素、舒适且实用。','结实鞋底适合岩石小径。')],M('It was sensible of Jo to sail into the storm without checking any warning or weather report.','It was sensible of Jo to check the storm warning before sailing.','不查看警报就驶入风暴不是明智做法。','meaning'),[q('What did Jo check before boating?','the storm warning','the semester calendar','the shoe seller’s receipt','乔出船前查看了风暴预警。',1,'context'),q('When can the factory finish the sensible repair plan?','before it reopens','after all available parts are discarded','only after the factory closes permanently','维修方案能在工厂重新开工前完成。',2,'context'),q('What does sensible mean about the shoes?','plain and comfortable for practical use','fashionable but painful','unrelated to the trail','此处 sensible 描述朴素实用、适合步行的鞋。',3,'meaning'),q('Which decision is sensible?','checking a storm warning before sailing','ignoring a storm warning and taking a boat out','wearing high heels on a rocky trail','出船前查看风暴警报是明智的选择。',1,'context')]);
P('sensitive','Sensitive comes from Latin sensitivus, from sentire (“feel”); it can mean easily affected, considerate of others, or able to detect small changes/needing care.',[C('sensitive.s1','敏感的；易受影响的','The sensitive microphone picked up even the faint hum of the refrigerator across the room.','这支灵敏的麦克风连房间另一侧冰箱微弱的嗡鸣声都收录到了。','The sensitive microphone picked up / even the faint hum / across the room.','sensitive.s1 指容易受刺激或影响的。','麦克风能检测到微弱声音。'),C('sensitive.s2','体贴的；善解人意的','A sensitive manager asked the employee privately about the bereavement instead of raising it at the team meeting.','体贴的经理私下询问员工丧亲情况，没有在团队会议上提起。','A sensitive manager asked privately / rather than raising it / at the team meeting.','sensitive.s2 指能体察他人感受且小心避免冒犯的。','经理顾及员工感受。'),C('sensitive.s3','灵敏的；需小心处理的','The sensitive instrument must remain level, because a slight tilt changes its measurements.','这台精密仪器必须保持水平，因为轻微倾斜就会改变测量结果。','The sensitive instrument must remain level / because a slight tilt / changes the measurements.','sensitive.s3 指能测出细微变化，或需要谨慎处理的。','仪器会受轻微倾斜影响。')],M('The sensitive manager announced the employee’s private bereavement details to the whole team without asking.','The sensitive manager asked about the bereavement privately and with care.','未经允许公开隐私不体贴他人感受。','meaning'),[q('What faint sound did the microphone detect?','the refrigerator’s hum','a stadium crowd from another city','a printed letter','麦克风收录到冰箱微弱的嗡鸣声。',1,'context'),q('How did the manager ask about the bereavement?','privately rather than at the team meeting','by announcing it to the entire office','by sending it to a newspaper','经理私下询问，没有在会议上谈及。',2,'context'),q('What does sensitive mean about the instrument?','able to register small changes or needing careful handling','unable to measure any change','unaffected by being tilted','仪器句中的 sensitive 指对细微变化灵敏、需小心使用。',3,'meaning'),q('What makes the manager sensitive?','considering the employee’s feelings and protecting privacy','telling everyone the employee’s private news','ignoring the employee’s loss','经理体察员工感受并保护其隐私，体现体贴。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sensitively','Sensitively is formed from sensitive and -ly; it means with care for other people’s feelings or with a strong response to slight stimuli.',C('sensitively.s1','体察入微地；敏感地','The counselor sensitively asked whether Noor wanted company before inviting other colleagues into the room.','辅导员体贴地询问努尔是否希望有人陪伴，然后才邀请其他同事进屋。','The counselor sensitively asked Noor / whether she wanted company / before inviting colleagues.','sensitively.s1 指顾及他人感受地，或对轻微刺激反应强烈地。','辅导员先征求努尔的意愿。'),M('The counselor sensitively respected Noor’s privacy by inviting every colleague into the room without asking her.','The counselor sensitively asked Noor’s permission before inviting colleagues.','未征求同意就公开隐私并不体贴。','meaning'),[q('What did the counselor ask Noor?','whether she wanted company','whether she would sell her office','whether the room was semiarid','辅导员询问努尔是否希望有人陪伴。',1,'context'),q('When were other colleagues invited in?','after Noor was asked','before the counselor arrived','without anyone entering the room','辅导员先询问努尔，然后才邀请同事进屋。',1,'context'),q('What does sensitively mean here?','with care for another person’s feelings','with no awareness of other people','in a way that ignores privacy','sensitively 在此指体察他人感受地。',1,'meaning'),q('Which response is sensitively given?','asking a grieving person whether they want visitors','announcing private news without permission','insisting that everyone discuss a loss publicly','先询问丧亲者是否愿意见人，属于 sensitively 的做法。',1,'context')]);
P('sensitivity','Sensitivity is formed from sensitive and -ity; it can mean susceptibility to hurt, thoughtful consideration of others, or plural sensitive topics.',[C('sensitivity.s1','敏感；易受伤','Her sensitivity to criticism made even a brief comment about the draft feel painful.','她对批评很敏感，连对草稿的一句简短意见都让她感到难受。','Her sensitivity to criticism made / a brief comment / feel painful.','sensitivity.s1 指容易因言语或事件而感到受伤、不安。','简短批评也令她难受。'),C('sensitivity.s2','体谅；得体','The interview showed sensitivity when the reporter asked permission before discussing the family’s loss.','记者在谈及这家人的丧亲之痛前先征求同意，体现了体谅。','The interview showed sensitivity / when the reporter asked permission / before discussing the loss.','sensitivity.s2 指行动前周到考虑他人感受的品质。','记者先征求家人同意。'),C('sensitivity.s3','敏感问题；忌讳（复数）','The moderator asked panelists to avoid the topic of recent layoffs because it was one of the meeting’s sensitivities.','主持人请嘉宾避开近期裁员这一话题，因为它是会议中的敏感事项之一。','The moderator asked panelists to avoid layoffs / because they were / meeting sensitivities.','sensitivity.s3 复数可指会令人不快、大家不愿讨论的敏感问题。','近期裁员是会议敏感话题。')],M('The reporter showed sensitivity by discussing the family’s loss publicly without first asking permission.','The reporter showed sensitivity by asking permission before discussing the family’s loss.','体谅要求先考虑对方感受并征求同意。','meaning'),[q('What made a brief comment painful for her?','her sensitivity to criticism','her lack of a draft','the reporter’s question about a price','她对批评敏感，所以简短意见也让她难受。',1,'context'),q('What did the reporter do before discussing the loss?','asked permission','announced it to the public','sent off a form','记者先征求同意。',2,'context'),q('What are “meeting sensitivities” in the layoffs example?','topics people may find upsetting and prefer not to discuss','the moderator’s five physical senses','a list of meeting attendees','此处 sensitivities 指会议中可能令人不安的敏感话题。',3,'meaning'),q('What does sensitivity mean in the reporter example?','thoughtful care for other people’s feelings','being easily hurt by every comment','a device that detects movement','此处 sensitivity 指体谅他人感受。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sensitize','Sensitize combines sense-related sensitive with -ize; it means cause a person, cell, or film to react more readily to a stimulus.',C('sensitize.s1','使具有敏感性','Repeated exposure to the chemical can sensitize the skin, making it react to even a small amount later.','反复接触这种化学品会使皮肤变得敏感，之后少量接触也可能引起反应。','Repeated exposure can sensitize the skin / making it react / to a small amount.','sensitize.s1 指使人、细胞或胶片更容易对刺激产生反应。','反复接触会增强皮肤反应。'),M('Repeated exposure to the chemical sensitized the skin so that it became less likely to react to it.','Repeated exposure sensitized the skin so that it reacted more readily.','sensitize 表示增强敏感性，反应性降低与词义相反。','meaning'),[q('What can repeated exposure do to the skin?','make it react to even a small amount','make it unable to detect any chemical','turn it into a semiconductor','反复接触会使皮肤对少量化学品也产生反应。',1,'context'),q('Which substance causes the reaction in the example?','the chemical','a red flag','a punctuation mark','例句中的化学品会使皮肤变得敏感。',1,'context'),q('What does sensitize mean?','cause something to react more readily to a stimulus','remove every ability to respond','make a surface completely molten','sensitize 指使某物更容易对刺激产生反应。',1,'meaning'),q('What might a sensitized cell do?','respond to a lower level of a stimulus','stop responding to every signal','become a university senate','被 sensitized 的细胞可能对更低强度的刺激产生反应。',1,'context')]);
P('sensor','Sensor comes from Latin sentire (“feel, perceive”) and -or; it is a device that measures light, heat, movement, or another quantity and sends the data to a computer.',C('sensor.s1','传感器；感应器','A motion sensor switched on the corridor lights when someone approached the laboratory door.','有人靠近实验室门时，运动传感器打开了走廊灯。','A motion sensor switched on the lights / when someone approached / the laboratory door.','sensor.s1 指测量光、热、运动等并把信息传给计算机的装置。','传感器检测到有人靠近。'),M('The motion sensor switched on the corridor lights by measuring the price of a novel.','The motion sensor detected movement near the door and switched on the lights.','运动传感器检测移动，不测量书价。','meaning'),[q('What did the motion sensor detect?','someone approaching the laboratory door','a change in the book’s price','a sentence in a seminar','传感器检测到有人靠近实验室门。',1,'context'),q('What happened after the sensor detected movement?','the corridor lights switched on','the door was sent abroad','the lights were permanently removed','检测到移动后走廊灯亮了。',1,'context'),q('What is a sensor?','a device that measures a quantity and passes the information on','a person who sends a letter','a punctuation mark between clauses','sensor 指测量并传递信息的装置。',1,'meaning'),q('Which device is a sensor?','a heat detector that sends temperature readings to a computer','a paper form mailed to a seller','a lamp with no measuring function','把温度读数传到电脑的热探测器是 sensor。',1,'context')]);
P('sensory','Sensory comes from Latin sensorius, from sensus (“perception”); it means connected with the senses or the nerves involved in sensation.',C('sensory.s1','感觉的；感官的','The sensory test asked volunteers to identify whether each fabric felt smooth, rough, warm, or cool.','感官测试让志愿者辨别每块布摸起来是光滑、粗糙、温暖还是凉爽。','The sensory test asked volunteers to identify / how each fabric felt / to touch.','sensory.s1 指与视觉、听觉、触觉、味觉、嗅觉或相关神经有关的。','志愿者通过触觉辨别织物。'),M('The sensory test measured the fabric’s color by asking volunteers to listen to it in darkness.','The sensory test asked volunteers to feel and describe the fabric.','听声音不能直接测量布料颜色；例句中的测试针对触觉。','meaning'),[q('What qualities did volunteers judge?','whether the fabrics felt smooth, rough, warm, or cool','how much each fabric sold for','which semicolon appeared on a page','志愿者辨别布料摸起来的质感与温度。',1,'context'),q('Which sense did the test mainly use?','touch','smell only','balance only','测试主要使用触觉。',1,'context'),q('What does sensory mean?','connected with the senses or their nerves','unrelated to perception','able to govern a university','sensory 指与感官或感觉神经有关。',1,'meaning'),q('Which task is sensory?','identifying a fabric by feeling its texture','calculating a seller’s annual profit','arranging chairs in a semicircle','通过触摸辨别织物质地属于 sensory task。',1,'context')]);
P('sensual','Sensual comes from Latin sensualis, from sensus (“feeling”); it concerns physical pleasures rather than intellectual or spiritual ones.',C('sensual.s1','肉体快感的','The novel describes the sensual pleasure of warm sunlight and soft music without suggesting anything harmful.','这部小说描写了温暖阳光与柔和音乐带来的感官愉悦，并无不当暗示。','The novel describes sensual pleasure / from warm sunlight / and soft music.','sensual.s1 指与身体感官享受有关，而非智力或精神活动。','描写阳光和音乐带来的身体感受。'),M('The passage was sensual because it discussed abstract logic while avoiding all bodily sensations.','The passage was sensual because it described physical pleasure from sunlight and music.','只谈抽象逻辑而回避身体感受，不属于 sensual。','meaning'),[q('What physical experiences does the novel describe?','warm sunlight and soft music','the cost of a senate bill','a motion sensor’s readings','小说描写阳光与音乐带来的感官体验。',1,'context'),q('What kind of pleasure is emphasized?','pleasure experienced through the body and senses','pleasure from solving a legal equation only','pleasure from winning a promotion','例句强调身体感官带来的愉悦。',1,'context'),q('What does sensual mean?','connected with physical pleasures','connected only with abstract reasoning','easily measuring a small stimulus','sensual 指与身体快感有关。',1,'meaning'),q('Which description is sensual?','the comforting warmth of a bath and the taste of fruit','a proof about the structure of a sentence','a report of an employee’s seniority','温泉的暖意和水果的味道属于 sensual experience。',1,'context')]);
P('sensuous','Sensuous is formed from sense and -uous; it describes something that appeals richly and pleasantly to the senses.',C('sensuous.s1','感官上愉悦的','The chef created a sensuous dessert with crisp pastry, fragrant citrus, and smooth cream.','厨师制作了一款感官体验丰富的甜点，结合了酥脆糕皮、芬芳柑橘和细滑奶油。','The chef created a sensuous dessert / with crisp pastry / fragrant citrus, and smooth cream.','sensuous.s1 指以丰富、愉悦的方式吸引感官。','甜点兼有口感、香气和质地。'),M('The dessert was sensuous because it had no taste, smell, texture, or other sensory appeal.','The dessert was sensuous because its taste, fragrance, and texture appealed to the senses.','毫无感官吸引力与 sensuous 的含义相反。','meaning'),[q('Which flavors or qualities did the dessert combine?','crisp pastry, fragrant citrus, and smooth cream','a cold metal railing and a loud alarm','a list of senate members','甜点结合了酥脆糕皮、芬芳柑橘和细滑奶油。',1,'context'),q('What made the dessert appealing?','its texture, fragrance, and taste','its lack of any sensory quality','its low price alone','甜点的口感、香气和味道带来感官吸引力。',1,'context'),q('What does sensuous mean?','appealing richly and pleasantly to the senses','having no connection with the senses','concerned only with a legal punishment','sensuous 指以丰富愉悦的方式吸引感官。',1,'meaning'),q('Which scene is sensuous?','a fragrant garden with vivid colors and textured leaves','a blank room with no smell, sound, or detail','a list of punctuation rules','有香气、鲜艳颜色和不同叶片质地的花园很 sensuous。',1,'context')]);
P('sentence','Sentence comes through Old French from Latin sententia (“opinion, thought”); it can mean a group of words expressing a complete idea, a court’s punishment, or to impose that punishment.',[C('sentence.s1','句子','“The train arrived early” is a sentence because it expresses a complete idea.','“火车提前到达了”是一个句子，因为它表达了完整意思。','“The train arrived early” is a sentence / because it expresses / a complete idea.','sentence.s1 指表达完整意思的一组词。','句子有完整表达。'),C('sentence.s2','判决；刑期','The judge reduced the prisoner’s sentence after reviewing evidence of his cooperation.','法官审查其配合调查的证据后，减轻了囚犯的刑期。','The judge reduced the prisoner’s sentence / after reviewing / evidence of cooperation.','sentence.s2 指法院判给有罪者的惩罚。','法官调整了刑罚。'),C('sentence.s3','判决；宣判','The court sentenced the fraudster to three years in prison after the jury returned its verdict.','陪审团作出裁决后，法院判处这名诈骗犯三年监禁。','The court sentenced the fraudster / to three years / after the verdict.','sentence.s3 作动词，指在法庭上宣告某人的刑罚。','法院宣告刑罚。')],M('The judge sentenced the prisoner to a written group of words that expressed a complete idea.','The judge sentenced the prisoner to a term of imprisonment.','法院 sentence 某人是判处刑罚，不是给出语法句子。','meaning'),[q('Why is “The train arrived early” a sentence?','it expresses a complete idea','it states a court’s punishment','it contains no verb','该组词表达完整意思，因此是句子。',1,'context'),q('What happened to the prisoner’s sentence?','the judge reduced it','the jury mailed it to the court','the prisoner used it as a semicolon','法官审查证据后减轻了囚犯的刑期。',2,'context'),q('What does sentence mean as a verb in the court example?','to state in court what punishment someone will receive','to arrange words into a complete idea','to forward a letter to someone','sentence 作动词指宣告刑罚。',3,'meaning'),q('What is a sentence in grammar?','a group of words expressing a complete idea','a court punishment after conviction','a person’s opinion alone','语法中的 sentence 是表达完整意思的一组词。',1,'meaning')]);
P('sentient','Sentient comes from Latin sentire (“feel, perceive”); it describes a being capable of sensing and feeling, not merely reacting mechanically.',C('sentient.s1','有感觉能力的','The debate asked whether a sentient animal could feel pain, rather than merely react to a stimulus like a machine.','这场辩论探讨有感觉能力的动物是否会感到疼痛，而不只是像机器那样对刺激作出反应。','The debate asked whether a sentient animal could feel pain / rather than merely react / like a machine.','sentient.s1 指能够感知和感受，而不只是机械反应的。','讨论区分感受疼痛与机械响应。'),M('A thermostat is sentient because it reacts to heat, even though it cannot feel or perceive anything.','A sentient being can experience feeling, unlike a thermostat that only reacts mechanically.','机械装置的反应本身不表示它有感受能力。','meaning'),[q('What ability did the debate ask about?','whether an animal could feel pain','whether a thermostat could measure price','whether a sentence had a semicolon','讨论关注动物是否能感受到疼痛。',1,'context'),q('What distinction did the debate make?','feeling versus merely mechanical reaction','selling versus buying','a semester versus a year','辩论区分真正感受与机械反应。',1,'context'),q('What does sentient mean?','capable of sensing and feeling','able only to react mechanically','having a high rank in a senate','sentient 指能感知并产生感受。',1,'meaning'),q('Which being is sentient in the example’s contrast?','an animal able to experience pain','a thermostat that only responds to heat','a motion sensor that switches on lights','能体验疼痛的动物具有 sentience。',1,'meaning')]);
P('sentiment','Sentiment comes through French sentiment from sentir (“feel”); it can mean an emotion, an opinion about what is right, or tender/sad feeling.',[C('sentiment.s1','情绪；感情','A sentiment of gratitude spread through the room when the volunteers returned after the flood.','洪灾后志愿者们回来时，房间里充满了感激之情。','A sentiment of gratitude spread / through the room / when volunteers returned.','sentiment.s1 指怜悯、爱或悲伤等感情。','人们对志愿者心怀感激。'),C('sentiment.s2','观点；意见','Her sentiment was that public parks should remain free for families who cannot afford private clubs.','她的观点是，公共公园应继续向负担不起私人俱乐部的家庭免费开放。','Her sentiment was that parks should remain free / for families / unable to afford clubs.','sentiment.s2 指基于个人判断或价值观的意见。','她表达了有关公园政策的观点。'),C('sentiment.s3','伤感；多愁善感','The old song filled him with sentiment, and he grew tearful remembering his childhood home.','这首老歌令他伤感起来，让他想起童年故居时眼眶湿润。','The old song filled him with sentiment / and made him tearful / about his childhood home.','sentiment.s3 指可能显得过度的温柔或悲伤情绪。','歌曲引起对童年的伤感回忆。')],M('Her sentiment was that public parks should close to families because she believed access should be free.','Her sentiment was that public parks should remain free for families.','观点内容被写成与说明相反。','meaning'),[q('What feeling filled the room when volunteers returned?','gratitude','anger at the patients','fear of a semester','志愿者回来时，房间里充满了感激。',1,'context'),q('What was her opinion about public parks?','they should remain free for families','they should be replaced by private clubs','they should close after every flood','她认为公共公园应继续对家庭免费开放。',2,'context'),q('What does sentiment mean in the old-song example?','a tender or sad feeling','a court’s punishment','a scientific measurement','老歌引发的 sentiment 指温柔或悲伤的情绪。',3,'meaning'),q('What does sentiment mean in “Her sentiment was that parks should remain free”?','an opinion about what is right','a physical feeling in the fingers','a message sender','此处 sentiment 指她对公园政策的观点。',2,'meaning')]);
P('sentimental','Sentimental is formed from sentiment and -al; it can mean tenderly sad or loving, overly controlled by emotion, or kept for happy memories.',[C('sentimental.s1','感伤的；多愁善感的','The sentimental farewell brought tears to several coworkers as they recalled years of shared projects.','这场感伤的告别让几位同事落泪，他们回忆起多年共同完成的项目。','The sentimental farewell brought tears / as coworkers recalled / shared projects.','sentimental.s1 指流露温柔、爱意或悲伤情感的。','告别唤起温柔而悲伤的回忆。'),C('sentimental.s2','感情用事的','The reviewer called the decision sentimental because it ignored the budget evidence and followed emotion alone.','评论者称这项决定感情用事，因为它忽视预算证据、只凭情绪行事。','The reviewer called the decision sentimental / because it ignored the evidence / and followed emotion alone.','sentimental.s2 贬义用法指让感情过度支配判断。','决定只听情绪而忽略证据。'),C('sentimental.s3','有感情价值的；念旧的','He kept the sentimental ticket from his first concert because it reminded him of a happy evening.','他保留了第一次听演唱会的票根，因为它让他想起一个愉快的夜晚。','He kept the sentimental ticket / because it reminded him / of a happy concert.','sentimental.s3 指因使人想起快乐往事而被保留的物品。','票根承载愉快回忆。')],M('The sentimental decision followed the budget evidence carefully and ignored every emotional appeal.','The sentimental decision followed emotion while ignoring the budget evidence.','只按证据而忽略情绪，不符合这里的贬义用法。','meaning'),[q('What made coworkers emotional at the farewell?','memories of years of shared projects','the ticket price for a future concert','the annual budget report','同事回忆多年共同项目时在告别会上落泪。',1,'context'),q('Why did he keep the old ticket?','it reminded him of a happy evening','it proved the budget was balanced','it was a current travel document','票根让他想起愉快的演出夜晚。',3,'context'),q('What does sentimental mean in the reviewer’s criticism?','letting emotion control judgment too much','carefully following budget evidence','having no emotional response','评论者批评的 sentimental 指感情过度支配判断。',2,'meaning'),q('What does sentimental mean about the saved ticket?','kept because it recalls happy times','kept because it has no personal meaning','kept as evidence in a court sentence','票根因让人想起快乐往事而被保留，属于 sentimental。',3,'meaning')]);
P('sentimentalism','Sentimentalism is formed from sentimental and -ism; it means excessive emotion, especially emotion viewed as shallow or self-indulgent.',C('sentimentalism.s1','滥情；感伤倾向','The critic objected to the novel’s sentimentalism, saying every scene forced tears without earning the reader’s sympathy.','评论家反对小说的滥情，认为每个场景都硬要煽泪，却没有赢得读者的同情。','The critic objected to sentimentalism / because each scene forced tears / without earning sympathy.','sentimentalism.s1 指被认为肤浅或自我沉溺的过度情绪表达。','情绪煽动没有得到情节铺垫。'),M('The critic accused the novel of sentimentalism because it restrained emotion and relied only on measured evidence.','The critic accused the novel of sentimentalism because it forced excessive emotion without earning sympathy.','克制情绪、只依据证据不符合过度煽情。','meaning'),[q('What did the critic say the scenes did?','forced tears without earning sympathy','proved every claim with evidence','removed all emotional language','评论者认为场景硬煽眼泪，却没有赢得同情。',1,'context'),q('What style did the critic object to?','excessive emotion','careful scientific measurement','a semicircular arrangement','评论者反对的是小说的过度感伤。',1,'context'),q('What is sentimentalism?','excessive emotion viewed as shallow or self-indulgent','complete absence of feeling','a careful study of signs','sentimentalism 指被认为肤浅或自我沉溺的过度情绪。',1,'meaning'),q('Which passage might be criticized for sentimentalism?','one that repeatedly demands tears without developing the characters','one that presents restrained emotion and detailed evidence','one that defines a punctuation mark','反复强求读者流泪却缺乏人物铺垫的段落可能被批评为 sentimentalism。',1,'context')]);
P('sentimentality','Sentimentality is formed from sentimental and -ity; it means excessive tenderness or emotion, particularly in a story or artwork.',C('sentimentality.s1','多愁善感；感情用事','The film’s final scene avoided sentimentality by letting the siblings reconcile quietly without swelling music.','电影结尾没有煽情，只让兄妹安静和解，没有配上逐渐高涨的音乐。','The final scene avoided sentimentality / by letting the siblings reconcile quietly / without swelling music.','sentimentality.s1 指故事或艺术作品中过度的温情或情绪表达。','克制的和解避免了过度煽情。'),M('The film showed sentimentality by avoiding every emotional cue and presenting the reunion in a detached, factual way.','The film risked sentimentality by using excessive emotional cues in the reunion.','毫无情绪渲染与过度煽情相反。','meaning'),[q('How did the siblings reconcile?','quietly, without swelling music','with a loud choir and repeated tears','by refusing to meet','兄妹安静和解，没有配上煽情音乐。',1,'context'),q('What did the ending avoid?','excessive emotional cues','the family reunion itself','a complete sentence','结尾避免了过度的情绪渲染。',1,'context'),q('What does sentimentality mean?','excessive tenderness or emotion in a work','a lack of any artistic feeling','an opinion about public parks','sentimentality 指作品中过度的温情或情绪。',1,'meaning'),q('Which ending risks sentimentality?','one that piles on music and tears to force an emotional response','one that shows a quiet reunion without emotional cues','one that states the date plainly','用音乐和眼泪强行煽动情绪的结尾可能显得 sentimentality 过度。',1,'context')]);
P('sentimentalize','Sentimentalize is formed from sentimental and -ize; it means treat or write about something in an excessively emotional way.',C('sentimentalize.s1','把……写得感伤','The historian refused to sentimentalize the strike and included both its achievements and its difficult costs.','历史学家拒绝把这场罢工写得过分感伤，同时写出了其成就与沉重代价。','The historian refused to sentimentalize the strike / and included / achievements and costs.','sentimentalize.s1 指以过度感伤的方式看待或书写某事。','历史叙述兼顾成就与代价。'),M('The historian sentimentalized the strike by describing every hardship with detached figures and no emotion.','The historian sentimentalized the strike by dwelling on emotional memories and omitting its costs.','只列客观数字、不渲染情绪并非过度感伤。','meaning'),[q('What did the historian include in the account?','both achievements and difficult costs','only happy memories','only the strike’s final date','历史学家写出了罢工的成就与沉重代价。',1,'context'),q('What did the historian refuse to do?','write about the strike in an excessively emotional way','mention the strike’s costs','include any historical facts','历史学家拒绝把罢工写得过分感伤。',1,'context'),q('What does sentimentalize mean?','treat or write about something in an overly emotional way','record every event without emotion','make a subject semiarid','sentimentalize 指过度感伤地看待或书写某事。',1,'meaning'),q('Which account sentimentalizes an event?','one that dwells on emotional memories and omits real costs','one that describes achievements and costs together','one that lists dates and evidence plainly','只渲染情绪回忆而略去真实代价的叙述属于 sentimentalize。',1,'context')]);
P('sentry','Sentry comes through French sentinelle from Italian sentinella (“watch”); it means a soldier stationed to guard a gate or other entrance.',C('sentry.s1','岗哨；哨兵','A sentry stood beside the north gate and checked each vehicle entering the military base.','一名哨兵站在北门旁，检查每辆进入军事基地的车辆。','A sentry stood beside the north gate / and checked / each entering vehicle.','sentry.s1 指被安排在入口处值守警戒的士兵。','哨兵在基地入口检查车辆。'),M('The sentry left the gate unguarded and invited every unknown vehicle to enter without inspection.','The sentry guarded the gate and checked vehicles entering the base.','放弃警戒并不检查车辆与守卫职责相反。','meaning'),[q('Where did the sentry stand?','beside the north gate','inside the spring semester','at the auction platform','哨兵站在军事基地北门旁。',1,'context'),q('What did the sentry check?','each vehicle entering the base','the meaning of a poem','the sensor’s temperature reading','哨兵检查每辆进入基地的车辆。',1,'context'),q('What is a sentry?','a soldier posted to guard an entrance','a person who sells goods','a university governing council','sentry 指被安排在入口处警戒的士兵。',1,'meaning'),q('Which worker is a sentry?','a soldier watching a gate and checking arrivals','a senator voting on a bill','a seller offering a map','在门口值守并检查来者的士兵是 sentry。',1,'context')]);
P('sepal','Sepal is a botanical term formed from French sépale, ultimately related to Greek skepē (“covering”); it names one segment of a flower’s outer whorl.',C('sepal.s1','花萼的一片','The green sepals protected the unopened rosebud before its petals spread in the sun.','花瓣在阳光下展开之前，绿色花萼片保护着尚未开放的玫瑰花蕾。','The green sepals protected the rosebud / before its petals / spread in the sun.','sepal.s1 指花外轮中通常为绿色的一片。','花萼片在花苞开放前起保护作用。'),M('The botanist called a petal a sepal even though the part formed the colorful inner whorl of the flower.','The botanist identified the green outer floral segment as a sepal.','花瓣通常属于花冠；花萼片位于花的外轮。','meaning'),[q('What did the sepals protect?','the unopened rosebud','the fully grown sequoia','the senator’s report','花萼片保护尚未开放的玫瑰花蕾。',1,'context'),q('What color were the sepals?','green','bright blue','transparent like glass','例句中的花萼片是绿色的。',1,'context'),q('What is a sepal?','a segment of the outer whorl of a flower','the colorful inner petal of every flower','a seed in a semiconductor','sepal 指花外轮中的一片，通常为绿色。',1,'meaning'),q('Which part is a sepal?','a green outer segment protecting a flower bud','a red petal forming the inner whorl','a leaf from a giant evergreen tree','保护花蕾的绿色外轮部分是 sepal。',1,'context')]);
P('separable','Separable comes from Latin separabilis, from separare (“divide”); it means capable of being divided or detached.',C('separable.s1','可分离的','The toy’s wooden sections are separable, so each piece can be cleaned without soaking the whole model.','这件玩具的木质部分可以拆开，因此不用浸泡整个模型就能分别清洁。','The wooden sections are separable / so each piece / can be cleaned alone.','separable.s1 指能够被分开或拆卸的。','模型各部分可拆开清洁。'),M('The toy’s sections were separable even though they had been permanently glued into one solid block.','The toy’s sections were separable because each could be detached for cleaning.','永久粘成整体的部件无法拆开。','meaning'),[q('Why were the toy’s pieces separated for cleaning?','each wooden section could be detached','the whole model had to be soaked together','the pieces were welded into one block','玩具木质部分可以拆开单独清洁。',1,'context'),q('What could be cleaned without soaking the entire model?','each individual piece','only the box it came in','the glue after it dried permanently','每个部件都可以单独清洁。',1,'context'),q('What does separable mean?','capable of being divided or detached','permanently joined and impossible to split','made from a green flower part','separable 指能够分开或拆卸。',1,'meaning'),q('Which object is separable?','a model whose sections detach for washing','a single block of wood with no joints','a sealed item that cannot be opened','部件可以拆卸清洗的模型是 separable。',1,'context')]);
P('separate','Separate comes from Latin separare (“set apart”), from se- (“apart”) and parare (“prepare”); it can describe things apart, the act of dividing, or a couple ending shared life.',[C('separate.s1','分开的；单独的；不同的','The two laboratories use separate entrances, so visitors do not pass through the sterile testing room.','两个实验室使用不同入口，访客不必穿过无菌测试室。','The laboratories use separate entrances / so visitors do not pass / through the testing room.','separate.s1 形容彼此分开、不共用或不同的。','实验室入口互不相同。'),C('separate.s2','使分开；分隔','A low divider separates the quiet reading area from the noisy workshop.','一道矮隔板把安静的阅读区与嘈杂的工作间隔开。','A low divider separates the reading area / from the noisy / workshop.','separate.s2 作动词，指把人或事物分开或隔开。','隔板分隔两个区域。'),C('separate.s3','分手；分居','After months of trying to resolve their conflict, the couple decided to separate and live in different homes.','尝试数月解决冲突后，这对伴侣决定分居，搬到不同的住所。','The couple decided to separate / and live / in different homes.','separate.s3 指伴侣停止共同生活或分开。','两人决定分居。')],M('The divider separates the reading area from the workshop by joining both rooms into one shared space.','The divider separates the areas by keeping the reading space apart from the workshop.','连接成同一空间会取消分隔，不是 separate。','meaning'),[q('Which entrances do visitors use?','separate entrances for the two laboratories','one shared doorway through the testing room','the same door into the workshop','两个实验室各自使用不同入口。',1,'context'),q('What divides the reading area from the workshop?','a low divider','a shared table joining the rooms','a green sepal','一道矮隔板把两个区域隔开。',2,'context'),q('What does separate mean about the couple?','they stopped living together','they used different entrances at work','they divided the laboratory samples','separate 描述伴侣时指分居或分开生活。',3,'meaning'),q('What does separate mean as a verb here?','divide or keep two areas apart','join two rooms into one','sell an item to another country','隔板句中的 separate 指把区域隔开。',2,'meaning')]);
P('separately','Separately is formed from separate and -ly; it means in a separate way, not together with another person or thing.',C('separately.s1','分开地；各自地','Please submit the two grant applications separately because each belongs to a different review panel.','请分别提交两份资助申请，因为它们分别属于不同的评审组。','Submit the grant applications separately / because each belongs / to a different panel.','separately.s1 指彼此分开而非一起地。','每份申请由不同小组审查。'),M('The two applications were submitted separately in a single combined file for the same review panel.','The two applications were submitted separately to their different review panels.','合并在同一文件提交不符合分别提交。','meaning'),[q('Why should the applications be submitted separately?','each belongs to a different review panel','both go to the exact same panel','one application has no reviewer','两份申请属于不同评审组，因此要分开提交。',1,'context'),q('How many applications are mentioned?','two','one','five hundred','例句提到两份资助申请。',1,'context'),q('What does separately mean?','in a separate way, not together','all at once as a single unit','in a higher rank','separately 指分开地、各自地。',1,'meaning'),q('Which instruction uses separately correctly?','send each form in its own envelope to its assigned office','put every form into one file for one office','leave all forms together without sorting','把每份表格分别寄到对应办公室，是分开处理。',1,'context')]);
P('separation','Separation comes from Latin separatio, from separare (“divide”); it can mean living apart or the process of dividing things so they do not touch.',[C('separation.s1','分离；分居','The couple’s separation began when they moved to different homes but continued arranging care for their children.','这对伴侣搬到不同住所后开始分居，但仍共同安排照顾孩子。','The couple’s separation began / when they moved / to different homes.','separation.s1 指伴侣分开生活或结束共同关系的状态、过程。','两人住在不同住所。'),C('separation.s2','分离；隔离','A layer of foam provides separation between the hot pipe and the wooden wall.','一层泡沫把热管道与木墙隔开。','A layer of foam provides separation / between the hot pipe / and the wooden wall.','separation.s2 指把物体分开或防止它们接触的过程。','泡沫隔离热管与木墙。')],M('The foam layer prevented separation by pressing the hot pipe directly against the wooden wall.','The foam layer provided separation between the hot pipe and the wooden wall.','直接接触没有形成隔离。','meaning'),[q('Where did the couple live during their separation?','in different homes','in the same room with no change','inside the foam insulation','伴侣分居后住在不同的住所。',1,'context'),q('What did the foam separate?','the hot pipe and the wooden wall','two grant review panels','the couple’s children','泡沫层隔开了热管道与木墙。',2,'context'),q('What does separation mean in the couple example?','living apart as a couple','a judge’s prison sentence','an order of events','伴侣句中的 separation 指分居。',1,'meaning'),q('What does separation mean in the insulation example?','the process of keeping two things apart','a couple moving into different homes','a series of film shots','隔热材料句中的 separation 指把两个物体隔开。',2,'meaning')]);
P('September','September comes from Latin September, from septem (“seven”), because it was the seventh month in the early Roman calendar.',C('September.s1','九月','The orchard opens its apple-picking weekend in September, after the fruit has ripened on the trees.','果实在树上成熟后，果园会在九月开放周末采摘活动。','The orchard opens its apple-picking weekend / in September / after the fruit ripens.','September.s1 指八月之后、十月之前的月份。','采摘活动在九月开放。'),M('The orchard’s September apple-picking weekend took place in the month between December and January.','The orchard’s apple-picking weekend took place in September, after August and before October.','十二月和一月之间不是九月。','meaning'),[q('When does the orchard open apple picking?','in September','in February','in December','果园在九月开放苹果采摘活动。',1,'context'),q('What happens to the apples before picking?','they ripen on the trees','they are frozen in a warehouse','they are sold as semicolons','苹果先在树上成熟。',1,'context'),q('Which month is September?','the month after August and before October','the month between December and January','the first month of spring everywhere','September 是八月之后、十月之前的月份。',1,'meaning'),q('Why was September named from a word for seven?','it was the seventh month in the early Roman calendar','it always has seven days','it was the seventh month of every modern calendar','September 的名字与它在古罗马早期历法中的第七月位置有关。',1,'meaning')]);
P('septic','Septic comes from Greek sēptikos (“putrefactive”), from sēpein (“make rotten”); it describes a wound contaminated with harmful bacteria, often forming pus.',C('septic.s1','感染化脓的','The nurse cleaned the septic wound and took a sample because the skin around it was swollen and producing pus.','伤口周围肿胀并有脓液，护士清洗了感染化脓的伤口并采集样本。','The nurse cleaned the septic wound / and took a sample / because it produced pus.','septic.s1 指被有害细菌污染并可能化脓的伤口。','肿胀和脓液提示伤口感染。','医学'),M('The nurse called the wound septic even though it was clean, uninfected, and had no swelling or pus.','The nurse treated the wound as septic because it was infected, swollen, and producing pus.','没有感染和脓液的清洁伤口不符合 septic。','meaning'),[q('What did the nurse clean?','the infected wound','the grant application','a sequoia branch','护士清洗了感染化脓的伤口。',1,'context'),q('What signs appeared around the wound?','swelling and pus','a clear semicircle','a calm sky','伤口周围肿胀并有脓液。',1,'context'),q('What does septic mean here?','contaminated with harmful bacteria','free of bacteria and inflammation','able to detect movement','septic 描述被有害细菌污染的伤口。',1,'meaning'),q('Which wound is septic?','an infected wound with swelling and pus','a clean wound that is healing without infection','a cut with no bacteria or inflammation','感染、肿胀并化脓的伤口是 septic。',1,'context')]);
P('sequence','Sequence comes from Latin sequentia, from sequi (“follow”); it can mean an order, a set of related events or shots, or arranging/testing items in order.',[C('sequence.s1','顺序；次序','The recipe gives the sequence for adding ingredients so the dough rises evenly.','食谱列出了加入配料的顺序，使面团均匀发酵。','The recipe gives the sequence / for adding ingredients / so the dough rises evenly.','sequence.s1 指事情发生或排列的先后顺序。','按步骤加料影响发酵结果。'),C('sequence.s2','一系列；连续镜头','The film’s opening sequence follows a runner through the city before introducing the main character.','影片开场的一组连续镜头跟随一名跑步者穿过城市，然后才介绍主角。','The film’s opening sequence follows a runner / through the city / before the main character appears.','sequence.s2 指依次出现的一系列事件或镜头。','开场由一组连续画面组成。'),C('sequence.s3','按顺序排列；测定序列','The lab sequenced the DNA fragments to determine the order of their genetic units.','实验室测定了DNA片段的序列，以确定其遗传单位的排列顺序。','The lab sequenced DNA fragments / to determine / the order of their units.','sequence.s3 作动词，指排列事物顺序或测定DNA单位的次序。','实验室测定遗传单位顺序。')],M('The recipe’s sequence placed the final baking step before the dough was mixed.','The recipe’s sequence placed mixing before baking.','把烘烤安排在搅拌之前，颠倒了正确步骤。','meaning'),[q('What did the recipe list?','the order for adding ingredients','the names of the film’s characters','the number of months in a year','食谱列出了加入配料的顺序。',1,'context'),q('What does the film opening sequence follow?','a runner moving through the city','the DNA fragments in a lab','a recipe being baked','开场镜头跟随跑步者穿过城市。',2,'context'),q('What did the lab do to the DNA fragments?','determined the order of their genetic units','mixed them into bread dough','sent them to a film theater','实验室测定了DNA遗传单位的排列顺序。',3,'context'),q('What does sequence mean as a noun in “the recipe gives the sequence”?','the order in which steps happen','a person who watches a gate','a court’s punishment','食谱句中的 sequence 指步骤先后顺序。',1,'meaning')]);
P('sequential','Sequential comes from sequence and -al; it describes parts that follow a fixed order, each after the one before it.',C('sequential.s1','按顺序的；连续的','The software requires sequential steps: users must verify their address before they can confirm payment.','软件要求按顺序操作：用户必须先验证地址，才能确认付款。','The software requires sequential steps / verify the address first / then confirm payment.','sequential.s1 指各部分按固定次序一个接一个进行的。','地址验证先于付款确认。'),M('The software’s sequential process allowed users to confirm payment before entering or verifying an address.','The sequential process requires users to verify the address before confirming payment.','先付款后验证地址颠倒了规定顺序。','meaning'),[q('What must users verify first?','their address','their payment receipt','the program’s source code','用户必须先验证地址。',1,'context'),q('What may users do after verification?','confirm payment','skip every later step','delete the address','验证地址后，用户可以确认付款。',1,'context'),q('What does sequential mean?','following a fixed order, one part after another','happening randomly with no order','taking place at the same instant','sequential 指按固定顺序一个接一个进行。',1,'meaning'),q('Which process is sequential?','verify identity, then approve access','approve access first and never check identity','perform all steps in a random order','先验证身份再批准访问属于 sequential process。',1,'context')]);
P('sequentially','Sequentially is formed from sequential and -ly; it means following one another in a particular order.',C('sequentially.s1','依次地；按顺序地','The clerk processed the numbered applications sequentially, beginning with the lowest number.','职员从最小编号开始，依次处理这些编号申请。','The clerk processed the applications sequentially / beginning / with the lowest number.','sequentially.s1 指一个接一个地按次序进行。','编号从小到大依次处理。'),M('The clerk processed the applications sequentially by choosing random numbers and repeatedly skipping the next one.','The clerk processed the applications sequentially from the lowest number upward.','随机跳号不是按顺序处理。','meaning'),[q('Which application did the clerk process first?','the one with the lowest number','the one with the highest number','a number selected at random each time','职员先处理编号最小的申请。',1,'context'),q('How did the clerk handle the rest?','one after another in numbered order','all at once without reading them','by repeatedly skipping the next item','职员按编号顺序一个接一个处理。',1,'context'),q('What does sequentially mean?','following one another in a particular order','in a random and unrelated way','all at precisely the same moment','sequentially 指依次按顺序地。',1,'meaning'),q('Which action occurs sequentially?','reading the numbered tickets from 1 upward','drawing tickets randomly and ignoring some','reading every ticket simultaneously','从1开始按号码依次读票是 sequentially。',1,'context')]);
P('sequester','Sequester comes from Latin sequestrare (“separate, hand over for safekeeping”); it means isolate something or take and hold property under legal authority.',[C('sequester.s1','使隔绝；隔离','The wildlife team sequestered the recovering birds in a quiet enclosure away from visitors.','野生动物团队把康复中的鸟隔离在远离游客的安静围栏里。','The team sequestered the birds / in a quiet enclosure / away from visitors.','sequester.s1 指把人或物与其他事物分开、隔绝。','鸟被安置在单独围栏。'),C('sequester.s1','查封；依法扣押','The court ordered officials to sequester the disputed funds until ownership was decided.','法院命令官员依法扣押有争议的资金，直到确定所有权。','The court ordered officials to sequester funds / until ownership / was decided.','sequester.s1 指依法取走并保管财产。','争议资金暂由法院保管。')],M('The court sequestered the disputed funds by paying them to one claimant before ownership was decided.','The court sequestered the disputed funds and held them until ownership was decided.','提前付给一方不是隔离保管争议财产。','meaning'),[q('Where were the recovering birds kept?','in a quiet enclosure away from visitors','in the public seminar room','inside the courthouse vault','鸟被隔离在远离游客的安静围栏里。',1,'context'),q('What happened to the disputed funds?','officials held them until ownership was decided','they were paid to one claimant immediately','they were sent abroad','法院命令暂时扣押争议资金。',1,'context'),q('What does sequester mean in the bird example?','isolate from others','sell at a particular price','arrange in a fixed sequence','鸟类例句中的 sequester 指使其隔离。',1,'meaning'),q('What does sequester mean in the court example?','take and hold property under legal authority','give disputed money to one side','send a letter to a new address','法院例句中的 sequester 指依法扣押并保管财产。',1,'meaning')]);
P('sequoia','Sequoia was named for Sequoyah (also called George Gist), a Cherokee scholar who created a writing system; it is a name for the coast redwood or giant sequoia.',C('sequoia.s1','巨杉；红杉','The trail passed a sequoia so wide that six hikers could barely reach around its trunk together.','步道经过一棵巨杉，树干粗到六名徒步者合抱也勉强够到。','The trail passed a sequoia / so wide that six hikers / barely reached around its trunk.','sequoia.s1 指海岸红杉或巨杉等巨大的常绿树。','巨杉树干十分粗壮。'),M('The guide identified the tiny annual flower as a sequoia even though it had no woody trunk and lasted one day.','The guide identified the huge evergreen tree as a sequoia.','一年生小花不是巨型常绿树。','meaning'),[q('How wide was the sequoia’s trunk?','six hikers could barely reach around it together','one hiker could cover it with a finger','it was narrower than a flower stem','六名徒步者合抱也勉强够到树干。',1,'context'),q('What kind of plant was on the trail?','a huge evergreen tree','a small annual flower','a semiarid grass','步道旁是一棵巨大的常绿树。',1,'context'),q('What is a sequoia?','a coast redwood or giant sequoia tree','a shrub that grows only in deserts','a device that measures heat','sequoia 指海岸红杉或巨杉。',1,'meaning'),q('Who was Sequoyah, after whom sequoia was named?','a Cherokee scholar who created a writing system','a Roman senator who named September','a scientist who invented semiconductors','sequoia 的名称纪念创造切罗基文字系统的学者 Sequoyah。',1,'meaning')]);
P('serene','Serene comes from Latin serenus (“clear, calm”); it can describe a peaceful person or place, or clear, calm weather or sky.',[C('serene.s1','宁静的；安详的','Despite the noisy station, the meditation room remained serene and free from disturbance.','尽管车站很吵，冥想室仍然宁静安详，没有受到干扰。','The meditation room remained serene / despite the noisy station / nearby.','serene.s1 指平静、安宁且不受烦扰的。','室内环境保持宁静。'),C('serene.s2','（天空）晴朗的','By dawn the clouds had cleared, leaving a serene sky above the valley.','到黎明时云层散去，山谷上空变得晴朗宁静。','The clouds cleared by dawn / leaving a serene sky / above the valley.','serene.s2 描写天空或天气时指晴朗平静、无云。','云散后天空晴朗。')],M('The meditation room was serene because alarms rang continuously and people rushed through it.','The meditation room was serene because it remained calm and undisturbed.','持续警报和人流意味着环境并不宁静。','meaning'),[q('What remained serene near the station?','the meditation room','the crowded ticket line','the noisy platform','车站旁的冥想室保持宁静。',1,'context'),q('What was the sky like after the clouds cleared?','serene and clear','stormy with heavy clouds','dark and smoky','云散后山谷上空晴朗宁静。',2,'context'),q('What does serene mean about the room?','calm, peaceful, and undisturbed','crowded and noisy','easily separated into pieces','room 的 serene 指宁静、不受干扰。',1,'meaning'),q('What does serene mean about the sky?','clear and calm','full of thunderclouds','covered by smoke','描述天空时 serene 指晴朗平静。',2,'meaning')]);
P('serenity','Serenity comes from Latin serenitas, from serenus (“calm, clear”); it means a calm, peaceful state of mind or place.',C('serenity.s1','宁静；沉着','The garden’s serenity returned after the fountain was repaired and the construction crew left.','喷泉修好、施工队离开后，花园恢复了宁静。','The garden’s serenity returned / after the fountain was repaired / and the crew left.','serenity.s1 指内心或地点的平静安宁状态。','施工噪声消失后，花园重新安静。'),M('The garden’s serenity returned when the construction crew began using loud drills beside the fountain.','The garden’s serenity returned after the noisy crew left.','施工噪声加剧不会带来宁静。','meaning'),[q('What had been repaired before the garden quieted?','the fountain','the north gate','the laboratory sensor','花园安静下来前，喷泉已修好。',1,'context'),q('What happened to the construction crew?','they left','they began drilling all night','they became the garden’s visitors','施工队离开后，花园恢复宁静。',1,'context'),q('What does serenity mean?','a calm and peaceful state','a loud and crowded gathering','a legal order to hold property','serenity 指平静安宁的状态。',1,'meaning'),q('Where might someone seek serenity?','in a quiet garden after construction ends','beside a running drill at a worksite','inside a crowded stadium during a final','施工结束后安静的花园可能让人感到 serenity。',1,'context')]);
P('serf','Serf comes through Old French serf from Latin servus (“slave”); it means a person historically bound to a landowner’s estate and unable to leave freely.',C('serf.s1','农奴','The museum’s account explained that a medieval serf had to work the lord’s land and could not freely leave the estate.','博物馆的说明指出，中世纪农奴必须为领主耕地，不能自由离开庄园。','A medieval serf had to work the land / and could not / freely leave the estate.','serf.s1 指过去被束缚在地主土地上、不能自由离开的劳动者。','农奴受庄园制度限制。'),M('The medieval serf freely owned the estate and could leave it whenever he chose.','The medieval serf was bound to the landowner’s estate and could not freely leave.','自由拥有土地并可随时离开，与农奴身份相反。','meaning'),[q('Whose land did the serf have to work?','the lord’s land','the senate’s garden','a seller’s market stall','农奴必须为领主耕地。',1,'context'),q('Could the serf freely leave the estate?','no','yes, at any time','only to become a senator','农奴不能自由离开庄园。',1,'context'),q('What was a serf?','a person historically bound to an estate','a soldier guarding a gate','a worker paid to sell goods abroad','serf 指历史上被束缚于庄园的农奴。',1,'meaning'),q('Which person fits the historical meaning of serf?','a laborer required to work an estate and not free to leave','a tenant who can move whenever they wish','a landowner who controls the estate','必须为庄园劳动且不能自由离开的劳动者是 serf。',1,'context')]);
P('sergeant','Sergeant comes through Old French sergent from Latin serviens (“serving”); it is a non-commissioned army officer or, in Britain, a police officer of middle rank.',[C('sergeant.s1','中士','The army sergeant checked the patrol roster and briefed the soldiers before they left the base.','军队中士检查了巡逻名单，并在士兵离开基地前向他们作简报。','The army sergeant checked the roster / and briefed the soldiers / before departure.','sergeant.s1 指军队中的士官军衔。','中士负责简报巡逻人员。'),C('sergeant.s2','巡佐；警长（英）','A British police sergeant supervised the station desk while the inspector attended court.','督察出庭期间，一名英国警长负责监督警局值班台。','A British police sergeant supervised the desk / while the inspector / attended court.','sergeant.s2 在英国警察体系中指中级警衔。','警长监督警局值班工作。')],M('The army sergeant was a commissioned general who commanded the entire national force.','The army sergeant was a non-commissioned officer who briefed the patrol.','中士不是统领全国军队的将军。','meaning'),[q('What did the army sergeant check?','the patrol roster','the September calendar','the greenhouse’s crop list','中士检查了巡逻名单。',1,'context'),q('Who supervised the British station desk?','a police sergeant','a university senator','a sentry at a military gate','督察出庭期间，警长监督警局值班台。',2,'context'),q('What is a sergeant in the army example?','a non-commissioned officer','the highest commissioned general','a university governing council','军队例句中的 sergeant 指士官。',1,'meaning'),q('What can sergeant mean in Britain’s police service?','an officer of middle rank','a civilian who reports a crime','a soldier guarding a gate','在英国警察体系中，sergeant 可指中级警衔。',2,'meaning')]);
P('serial','Serial comes from series and Latin series (“row, chain”); it can mean a story released in parts, repeated in a pattern, or arranged one after another.',[C('serial.s1','连续剧；连载作品','The magazine published the mystery as a serial, printing one new chapter in each monthly issue.','杂志以连载形式刊登这部悬疑故事，每月一期推出一章。','The magazine published the mystery as a serial / one chapter / in each issue.','serial.s1 指分成多部分连续出版或播出的故事。','每期刊出一章。'),C('serial.s2','连续的；一连串的','The serial complaints about the same broken elevator continued for several weeks.','关于同一部电梯故障的一连串投诉持续了好几周。','Serial complaints continued / about the same broken elevator / for weeks.','serial.s2 指按同一模式反复出现的。','投诉重复发生。'),C('serial.s3','顺序排列的；串行的','The printer processed the files in serial order, finishing one document before starting the next.','打印机按串行顺序处理文件，完成一份后才开始下一份。','The printer processed files in serial order / finishing one / before starting the next.','serial.s3 指一个接一个、按顺序进行或发送的。','文件依次处理而非并行。')],M('The printer processed files in serial order by printing every document at the same time in parallel.','The printer processed files in serial order by finishing each one before starting the next.','同时并行处理不属于串行顺序。','meaning'),[q('How often did the magazine publish a new chapter?','one in each monthly issue','all chapters on the same day','one every ten years','杂志每月一期刊登新的一章。',1,'context'),q('What did the serial complaints concern?','the same broken elevator','three unrelated new elevators','a quiet garden','一连串投诉都关于同一部故障电梯。',2,'context'),q('What does serial mean in the printer example?','one after another in order','all at once in parallel','released as a monthly story','打印机例句中的 serial 指按顺序一个接一个。',3,'meaning'),q('What is a serial in the magazine example?','a story issued in separate parts','a single standalone notice','a complaint sent to a station','杂志句中的 serial 指分期连载的故事。',1,'meaning')]);
P('serialize','Serialize is formed from serial and -ize; it means publish a work in successive installments.',C('serialize.s1','分期发表；连载','The journal will serialize the researcher’s memoir, publishing one section in each weekly issue.','期刊将分期发表研究者的回忆录，每周一期刊出一部分。','The journal will serialize the memoir / publishing one section / in each weekly issue.','serialize.s1 指把一部作品分成连续部分逐期发表。','回忆录按周刊分段刊出。'),M('The journal serialized the memoir by publishing the entire work in one issue and no later installments.','The journal serialized the memoir by publishing one section in each weekly issue.','一次性刊完而没有后续分期，不是连载。','meaning'),[q('How much of the memoir appears in each issue?','one section','the whole work every week','no part at all','期刊每周一期刊出回忆录的一部分。',1,'context'),q('How often will the journal publish a section?','weekly','once every decade','only after the memoir is forgotten','期刊每周刊出一部分。',1,'context'),q('What does serialize mean?','publish a work in successive installments','print a work only once in full','separate a couple into two homes','serialize 指分期连续发表作品。',1,'meaning'),q('Which plan will serialize a novel?','publishing one chapter in every monthly issue','printing the whole novel in one issue only','keeping the novel unpublished','每月一期刊出一章属于 serialize。',1,'context')]);
P('series','Series comes from Latin series (“row, chain”); it means a set of related events, books, or programs, or an electrical connection where current passes through each part.',[C('series.s1','系列；连续；一套','The museum planned a series of evening lectures on the history of the harbor.','博物馆计划举办一系列关于港口历史的晚间讲座。','The museum planned a series of lectures / on the harbor’s history / in the evening.','series.s1 指一组同类事件、书籍或节目。','多场相关讲座构成一个系列。'),C('series.s2','（电）串联','In a series circuit, current passes through each lamp along a single path.','在串联电路中，电流沿一条路径依次通过每盏灯。','In a series circuit, current passes through each lamp / along a single path.','series.s2 指电流依次通过各元件的连接方式。','电流经过每盏灯。')],M('In a series circuit, current bypassed every lamp and traveled along several independent paths.','In a series circuit, current passed through each lamp along one path.','串联电路中的电流依次经过各元件，不是多条独立路径。','meaning'),[q('What did the museum plan?','a series of evening lectures','a single lecture on sports','a seminar on semiconductor prices','博物馆计划举办一系列晚间讲座。',1,'context'),q('How does current flow in a series circuit?','through each lamp along a single path','through only the first lamp','along several independent paths','串联电路的电流沿一条路径经过每盏灯。',2,'context'),q('What does series mean in the museum example?','a set of related events','an electrical route through components','an isolated event with no relation to others','博物馆句中的 series 指一系列相关活动。',1,'meaning'),q('What does series mean in “series circuit”?','a connection where current passes through each part','a program broadcast in separate chapters','a sequence of lectures','series circuit 中 series 指电流逐个经过元件的连接方式。',2,'meaning')]);
})();
